{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-avoid-all-finite-punctures-with-erase-complement-and-punctured-nhds", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For a finite exceptional set, isolate one puncture by taking the complement of `F.erase z`, then intersect with `𝓝[≠] z`; this excludes the whole finite set at once and avoids induction.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "avoid-all-finite-punctures-with-erase-complement-and-punctured-nhds", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For a finite exceptional set, isolate one puncture by taking the complement of `F.erase z`, then intersect with `𝓝[≠] z`; this excludes the whole finite set at once and avoids induction.", :body {:boundary "The construction handles finite, topologically discrete punctures. It does not generalize unchanged to an exceptional set accumulating at `z`.", :capture-kind :runner-filter-construction-and-commit-witnessed, :scope {:language :lean4, :problem "Near a chosen `z ∈ F`, show a zero-filled function agrees eventually on `𝓝[≠] z` with the original function defined on `Fᶜ`, without inducting over the finite set."}, :rule "For a finite exceptional set, isolate one puncture by taking the complement of `F.erase z`, then intersect with `𝓝[≠] z`; this excludes the whole finite set at once and avoids induction.", :key-api ["Finset.isClosed" "eventually_nhdsWithin_iff" "Finset.mem_erase" "Filter.EventuallyEq.differentiableAt_iff"], :construction ["`F.erase z` is finite and therefore closed." "Because `z ∉ F.erase z`, the complement `((F.erase z : Finset ℂ) : Set ℂ)ᶜ` is a neighbourhood of `z`." "Restrict that neighbourhood to the punctured filter `𝓝[≠] z`." "A point in this intersection is neither `z` nor any point of `F.erase z`, hence is outside all of `F`." "Use the resulting eventual non-membership to establish eventual equality with the reciprocal and transfer differentiability."], :lean-shape ["Obtain the neighbourhood with `(F.erase z).isClosed.isOpen_compl.mem_nhds`." "Rewrite through `eventually_nhdsWithin_iff`." "Discharge membership using `Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨hwz, hwF⟩`." "Transfer differentiability with `Filter.EventuallyEq.differentiableAt_iff`."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :arc-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T14:48:12.677935372Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-avoid-all-finite-punctures-with-erase-complement-and-punctured-nhds"}}
