{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-build-an-Orlicz-bound-counterexample-from-a-borderline-power-singularity", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For entropy-controlled counterexamples, choose a singularity whose failed target norm becomes a standard borderline power, and use a nearby integrable power only to dominate the logarithmic entropy term.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Refute an implication from entropy/Orlicz dual control to square integrability on a finite interval.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "build-an-Orlicz-bound-counterexample-from-a-borderline-power-singularity", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For entropy-controlled counterexamples, choose a singularity whose failed target norm becomes a standard borderline power, and use a nearby integrable power only to dominate the logarithmic entropy term.", :body {:hook "Choose `g(x)=x⁻¹ᐟ²`: it is integrable, its square is the borderline nonintegrable `x⁻¹`, and its entropy can be dominated by the slightly stronger but integrable power `4x⁻³ᐟ⁴`.", :capture-kind :runner-counterexample-route-and-ground-control-full-file-axiom-verification, :problem-class "Refute an implication from entropy/Orlicz dual control to square integrability on a finite interval.", :key-api ["intervalIntegral.integrableOn_Ioo_rpow_iff" "Real.abs_log_mul_self_rpow_lt" "Real.add_one_le_exp" "Integrable.mono" "integral_mono_ae" "integral_add"], :witness {:declaration "ApmCanaries.A01A06.orlicz_bound_not_implies_L2", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-integrity :intact}, :route-correction {:classification :third-confirming-instance, :existing-memory-id "e-codexpilot-override-a-documented-proof-route-when-component-evidence-favors-another", :supplied-route "Use `x^(-3/4)` as the counterexample and separately discharge its logarithmic entropy integrability.", :implemented-route "Use `x^(-1/2)` as the counterexample and reserve `x^(-3/4)` for an integrable domination bound.", :boundary "This confirms evidence-based route correction; it does not make `x^(-3/4)` mathematically invalid as a possible witness."}, :rule "For entropy-controlled counterexamples, choose a singularity whose failed target norm becomes a standard borderline power, and use a nearby integrable power only to dominate the logarithmic entropy term.", :witness-shape {:function "g(x) = x^(-1/2) for x > 0, and 0 otherwise", :l1 "the exponent -1/2 is greater than -1", :not-l2 "g(x)^2 = x^(-1), the borderline divergent power", :entropy-dominator "4*x^(-3/4), whose exponent is greater than -1", :constant "A = ∫_[0,1] g*log(g) + 2"}, :boundary "This establishes failure of the `L²` conclusion for the file's `OrliczBound`; it does not characterize the sharp distribution tail implied by entropy control.", :how-to-apply ["Define `g x` by `x^(-1/2)` for `x > 0` and zero otherwise, keeping measurability and endpoint behavior explicit." "Use `integrableOn_Ioo_rpow_iff` to prove `g ∈ L¹(0,1)` and to refute integrability of `g² = x⁻¹`." "Define the entropy density `ent x = g x * log (g x)`." "Apply `Real.abs_log_mul_self_rpow_lt` with exponent `1/4` and factor the powers to obtain `|ent x| ≤ 4x⁻³ᐟ⁴` on `(0,1)`." "Use the integrability of `x⁻³ᐟ⁴` to prove the entropy integral is finite." "Derive the pointwise Young–Fenchel inequality `g*f ≤ exp f + g*log g` from `Real.add_one_le_exp (f - log g)`." "Set `A = ∫ ent + 2`; combine the admissibility bound `∫ exp f ≤ 1` with integral monotonicity, avoiding an unnecessary exact evaluation of the entropy integral."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T22:19:00.345165741Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-build-an-Orlicz-bound-counterexample-from-a-borderline-power-singularity"}}
