{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-close-a92J05-by-transferring-the-unit-disk-zero-count", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:kind :feedback, :name "close-a92J05-by-transferring-the-unit-disk-zero-count", :hook "close-a92J05-by-transferring-the-unit-disk-zero-count", :body {:hook "The degree-ten and inside/outside bookkeeping are complete; a92J05 now needs only the argument-principle transfer proving that `5z³` and `z¹⁰ + 5z³ + 2z + 1` have the same three zeros in the unit disk.", :residual-goal "(p.roots.filter (fun z => ‖z‖ < 1)).card = 3", :capture-kind :runner-narrowed-frontier-and-ground-control-verification, :rejected-shortcut "`ConstructionTargets/Rouche.lean` may not be imported as if complete while `zeroCountInClosedBall_add_eq` remains sorried; that would propagate `sorryAx` rather than close this frontier.", :proved-prefix ["`rouche_condition` proves the strict boundary inequality." "`p_no_roots_on_circle` excludes unit-circle roots." "`p_card_roots` proves ten total roots with multiplicity." "`roots_inside_add_outside` partitions all roots." "`roots_outside_card_eq_of_inside_card_eq` reduces the answer seven to the residual inside count three." "`ConstructionTargets.Rouche.rouche_homotopy_ne_zero_on_sphere` proves boundary nonvanishing along the straight-line homotopy."], :dominant-and-remainder {:dominant "g(z) = 5*z^3", :remainder "h(z) = z^10 + 2*z + 1", :boundary-estimate "On ‖z‖ = 1, ‖h(z)‖ ≤ 4 < 5 = ‖g(z)‖."}, :target-polynomial "p(z) = z^10 + 5*z^3 + 2*z + 1", :literature {:source "leanprover-community Zulip archive", :archive-path "116395-maths/Argument.20principle.json", :use-status :historical-gap-anchor, :contribution "The thread identifies argument-principle, residue, and winding-number infrastructure as the historical missing bridge.", :boundary "The thread does not itself supply the Lean construction."}, :how-to-apply ["Reuse the proved strict boundary estimate `‖z¹⁰ + 2z + 1‖ < ‖5z³‖` on `‖z‖ = 1`." "Instantiate the straight-line Rouché homotopy between `5z³` and the target polynomial." "Supply the missing theorem that total divisor count in the closed disk is invariant under an analytic homotopy nonzero on the boundary." "Identify the divisor count of `5z³` on the unit disk with three." "Relate the target polynomial's divisor count to `(p.roots.filter (fun z => ‖z‖ < 1)).card`; boundary roots are already excluded." "Feed the resulting inside count to the axiom-clean algebraic tail `roots_outside_card_eq_of_inside_card_eq`."], :missing-bridge "`ConstructionTargets.Rouche.zeroCountInClosedBall_add_eq` still contains `sorry`. Mathlib's divisor/Jensen API represents multiplicities but does not currently supply the unweighted argument-principle homotopy-invariance theorem needed to transfer the total count.", :frontier/kind :application-of-missing-argument-principle-bridge, :unblocks [{:ref/type :lean-theorem, :ref/id "roots_outside_unit_disk"}], :relation-to-existing-frontier {:memory-id "e-codexpilot-zeroCountInClosedBall-homotopy-invariant", :relation "The existing memory states the general missing homotopy-invariance theorem. This record fixes its exact a92J05 instantiation, residual multiset goal, proved downstream tail, and final divisor-to-roots bridge.", :not-a-duplicate "It does not restate the general theorem as a new Mathlib gap; it records the narrowed application leaf that remains after the current partial."}}, :runner-model :codex, :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :frontier-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T19:30:19.120659031Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5"