{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-combine-Schwarz-rigidity-with-power-series-uniqueness", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For a disk self-map expressed as identity plus a higher-order series, turn pointwise summability into a convergence-radius bound, use Schwarz rigidity to kill the summed tail, fill its value at the center by continuity, and invoke formal power-series uniqueness to kill its coefficients.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Show that every coefficient above the linear term vanishes when a pointwise-summable disk power series defines a disk self-map tangent to the identity.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "combine-Schwarz-rigidity-with-power-series-uniqueness", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For a disk self-map expressed as identity plus a higher-order series, turn pointwise summability into a convergence-radius bound, use Schwarz rigidity to kill the summed tail, fill its value at the center by continuity, and invoke formal power-series uniqueness to kill its coefficients.", :body {:capture-kind :runner-proof-route-faithfulness-check-and-ground-control-verification, :problem-class "Show that every coefficient above the linear term vanishes when a pointwise-summable disk power series defines a disk self-map tangent to the identity.", :key-api ["FormalMultilinearSeries.le_radius_of_tendsto" "FormalMultilinearSeries.hasFPowerSeriesOnBall" "FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars_sum_eq" "HasFPowerSeriesAt.eq_zero_of_eventually" "FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars_series_eq_zero"], :witness {:declaration "disk_selfmap_tangent_identity", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-integrity :intact}, :rule "For a disk self-map expressed as identity plus a higher-order series, turn pointwise summability into a convergence-radius bound, use Schwarz rigidity to kill the summed tail, fill its value at the center by continuity, and invoke formal power-series uniqueness to kill its coefficients.", :analytic-construction ["Use `p.hasFPowerSeriesOnBall` to obtain differentiability of `p.sum` on the unit disk." "Prove `z² * p.sum z = ∑' n, a (n+2) * z^(n+2)` with `FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars_sum_eq`, `tsum_mul_left`, and `pow_add`." "Define `f z = z + z² * p.sum z`." "The hypotheses make `f` a differentiable disk self-map fixing zero; the product rule gives `deriv f 0 = 1`." "Apply the equality case of Schwarz's lemma, here packaged as the local `disk_selfmap_deriv_one_eq_identity`, to obtain `f = id` on the disk."], :hypothesis-audit "The proof uses the stated `Summable` hypothesis only to obtain termwise convergence after scaling. It does not replace it with absolute summability.", :coefficient-series ["Set `c n = a (n+2)`." "Encode `c` as `p = FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars ℂ c`." "For every positive real radius `r < 1`, divide the assumed summable shifted series by `r²`." "Summability makes the scaled coefficient terms tend to zero; apply `p.le_radius_of_tendsto` and then `ENNReal.le_of_forall_nnreal_lt` to prove `1 ≤ p.radius`."], :coefficient-uniqueness ["Away from zero, `z² * p.sum z = 0` implies `p.sum z = 0`." "At zero, compare the punctured-neighbourhood zero limit with continuity of `p.sum` to fill the removable value." "Turn local eventual equality to zero into `p = 0` with `HasFPowerSeriesAt.eq_zero_of_eventually`." "Use `FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars_series_eq_zero` and undo the index shift to conclude `a n = 0` for every `n ≥ 2`."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T15:06:06.833608008Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-combine-Schwarz-rigidity-with-power-series-uniqueness"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-complete-diskwise-L1-to-compact-uniform-convergence-on-local-half-disks", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "When a convergence hypothesis is local on disks, prove uniform Cauchy convergence and pointwise identification on one smaller concentric disk at a time, then use the local-uniform API for compact globalization.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Upgrade diskwise `L¹` convergence of holomorphic functions to compact-uniform convergence, analyticity of the limit, and compact-uniform convergence of derivatives.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "complete-diskwise-L1-to-compact-uniform-convergence-on-local-half-disks", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "When a convergence hypothesis is local on disks, prove uniform Cauchy convergence and pointwise identification on one smaller concentric disk at a time, then use the local-uniform API for compact globalization.", :body {:hook "Work pointwise on `closedBall x (R/2)`: the disk-area inequality makes the sequence uniformly Cauchy there, diskwise `L¹` plus continuity identifies its pointwise limit, and Mathlib packages these local limits over compact subsets.", :capture-kind :frontier-memory-used-to-close-own-problem-and-ground-control-full-file-verification, :problem-class "Upgrade diskwise `L¹` convergence of holomorphic functions to compact-uniform convergence, analyticity of the limit, and compact-uniform convergence of derivatives.", :implementation-arcs ["Derive `IsFiniteMeasureOnCompacts` for the file's mapped complex volume from the underlying homeomorphism; do not remove or bypass the custom measure instance." "Prove closed-ball containment by the triangle inequality when a guessed `closedBall_mono` lemma does not exist." "Give `setIntegral_mono_set` inequalities explicitly when `gcongr` infers their order incorrectly." "Expose positivity of the disk-area denominator before field normalization."], :key-api ["UniformCauchySeqOn.tendstoUniformlyOn_of_tendsto" "tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_of_forall_exists_nhds" "tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_iff_forall_isCompact" "TendstoLocallyUniformlyOn.differentiableOn" "TendstoLocallyUniformlyOn.deriv" "Measure.IsFiniteMeasureOnCompacts.map"], :witness {:axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :declarations ["uniformCauchySeqOn_closedBall_half" "tendsto_of_L1ConvergesOnDisks_at" "tendstoUniformlyOn_of_L1_on_disks" "differentiableOn_of_L1_limit" "tendstoUniformlyOn_deriv_of_L1" "L1_disk_convergence_analytic_upgrade"], :all-file-declarations 17}, :rule "When a convergence hypothesis is local on disks, prove uniform Cauchy convergence and pointwise identification on one smaller concentric disk at a time, then use the local-uniform API for compact globalization.", :frontier-provenance {:used-memory "e-codexpilot-upgrade-diskwise-L1-convergence-to-local-uniform-convergence", :prerequisite-memory "e-codexpilot-lift-the-circle-submean-bound-to-a-disk-area-bound", :use "The first memory's half-disk route carried the proof; the second prevented rebuilding the already verified polar disk-area bridge."}, :boundary "The proof relies on the already established disk-area sub-mean inequality and on local finiteness of the chosen complex volume.", :how-to-apply ["For each `x ∈ Ω`, use openness to choose `R > 0` with `closedBall x R ⊆ Ω`." "Apply the verified disk-area sub-mean inequality to `f m - f n` and bound its integral by the two outer-disk `L¹` errors." "Deduce `UniformCauchySeqOn` on `closedBall x (R/2)`." "Independently identify `f n x → F x`: combine continuity of `F` on a small disk with the constant-centred disk-area inequality and diskwise `L¹` convergence." "Use `UniformCauchySeqOn.tendstoUniformlyOn_of_tendsto` to obtain uniform convergence on the half-radius disk." "Assemble local uniform convergence with `tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_of_forall_exists_nhds`." "Convert to convergence on each compact subset with `tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_iff_forall_isCompact`." "Use the resulting locally uniform limit to discharge analyticity and derivative convergence through the existing Weierstrass APIs."], :route-choice {:used "local concentric half-disks", :avoided "constructing a global finite cover before proving the local estimate", :reason "The local-uniform API performs the global compact packaging once a neighbourhood estimate is available at every point."}}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T23:10:01.852590138Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-complete-diskwise-L1-to-compact-uniform-convergence-on-local-half-disks"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-convert-unit-complex-coefficient-to-an-angle-rotation", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "A disk-map equality proof has reached `h z = c * z` with `‖c‖ = 1`, but the downstream statement requires the coefficient in the form `exp (I * α)`.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "A disk-map equality proof has reached `h z = c * z` with `‖c‖ = 1`, but the downstream statement requires the coefficient in the form `exp (I * α)`.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "convert-unit-complex-coefficient-to-an-angle-rotation", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "Choose `α = c.arg`. → Use the unit-norm hypothesis to simplify the leading `‖c‖` factor to 1. → Commute the scalar product in the exponential exponent from `c.arg * I` to `I * c.arg`. → Use the library equality in the direction required by the coefficient goal.", :body {:problem-class "A disk-map equality proof has reached `h z = c * z` with `‖c‖ = 1`, but the downstream statement requires the coefficient in the form `exp (I * α)`.", :proof-shape ["Choose `α = c.arg`." "Use the unit-norm hypothesis to simplify the leading `‖c‖` factor to 1." "Commute the scalar product in the exponential exponent from `c.arg * I` to `I * c.arg`." "Use the library equality in the direction required by the coefficient goal."], :boundary "The lemma supplies the polar representation of one complex coefficient; the preceding Schwarz specialization is what proves the function is multiplication by that coefficient.", :observed-use "The committed `exists_rotation` theorem takes `c = deriv h 0` after `eq_deriv_mul`.", :capture-kind :runner-narrated-and-commit-witnessed, :lemma "`Complex.norm_mul_exp_arg_mul_I`", :location "`Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Arg`", :library-statement "`‖x‖ * Complex.exp (x.arg * Complex.I) = x`."}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/cron-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-28T14:53:40.527107354Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-convert-unit-complex-coefficient-to-an-angle-rotation"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-count-polynomial-lemniscate-components-by-roots-plus-one-exterior", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "Count complementary components by separating bounded interior pieces from the common unbounded exterior: inject interior components into algebraic witnesses and reserve one marker for the exterior.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Bound the number of connected components of the complement of the polynomial lemniscate `{z | ‖p(z)‖ = 1}` by `natDegree p + 1`.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "count-polynomial-lemniscate-components-by-roots-plus-one-exterior", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "Count complementary components by separating bounded interior pieces from the common unbounded exterior: inject interior components into algebraic witnesses and reserve one marker for the exterior.", :body {:hook "For `{‖p‖ = 1}`, count complement components by injecting bounded `{‖p‖ < 1}` pieces into roots and proving all `{1 < ‖p‖}` pieces meet one path-connected exterior.", :capture-kind :runner-sibling-transplant-ground-control-statement-comparison-and-axiom-verification, :problem-class "Bound the number of connected components of the complement of the polynomial lemniscate `{z | ‖p(z)‖ = 1}` by `natDegree p + 1`.", :key-api ["isOpen_connectedComponent" "IsEmbedding.closure_eq_preimage_closure_image" "IsPathConnected.preimage_coe" "Polynomial.isProperMap_eval" "Polynomial.tendsto_norm_atTop" "Nat.card_le_card_of_injective" "Polynomial.card_roots'"], :witness {:declaration "ApmCanaries.A01A08.connectedComponents_complement_lemniscate_le", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-integrity :character-identical-to-proved-sibling, :first-transplant-compile true}, :sublevel-route ["Polynomial properness bounds the whole sublevel set, hence every sublevel component." "If a bounded sublevel component contained no root, `1/p` would be analytic there, have boundary norm one, and have norm greater than one inside; maximum modulus gives a contradiction." "Choose one enclosed root per sublevel component." "If two components choose the same root, component maximality at their common point identifies the components, so root selection is injective."], :superlevel-route ["A superlevel component cannot be bounded: on its frontier `‖p‖ = 1`, while inside `‖p‖ > 1`, contradicting maximum modulus for a bounded component." "`Polynomial.isProperMap_eval` and polynomial growth provide a radius `R` beyond which every point is superlevel." "The strict radial exterior `{z | R < ‖z‖}` is path connected." "Every unbounded superlevel component meets this common exterior, hence any two such components agree."], :rule "Count complementary components by separating bounded interior pieces from the common unbounded exterior: inject interior components into algebraic witnesses and reserve one marker for the exterior.", :boundary "This construction uses the complex plane's connected radial exterior, polynomial properness, and the maximum/minimum modulus principles. It is not a general component-count theorem for arbitrary level sets or arbitrary noncompact spaces.", :how-to-apply ["Represent each connected component of the complement as an open connected subset of the ambient plane, with frontier contained in the level set." "Use connectedness and avoidance of the level set to classify each component entirely as `‖p(z)‖ < 1` or entirely as `1 < ‖p(z)‖`." "For a sublevel component, use polynomial properness to make it bounded and the minimum-modulus argument for `1/p` to obtain a root inside it." "For a superlevel component, rule out boundedness by maximum modulus." "Use `‖p(z)‖ → ∞` to put the complement of a sufficiently large ball inside the superlevel set; prove that radial exterior path connected, so all superlevel components coincide." "Inject components into `roots(p).toFinset ⊕ Unit`: a sublevel component maps to one chosen enclosed root, while the unique superlevel component maps to the unit marker." "Bound the root side by `natDegree p` and add the single exterior marker."], :final-count "The component tag lands in the disjoint sum of the distinct roots and `Unit`; `Nat.card_le_card_of_injective` and the root-cardinality bound yield at most `natDegree p + 1`. Constant-polynomial cases are split off.", :reuse-provenance {:source-problem "a00J04", :reuse-kind :character-identical-sibling-transplant, :verification ["Ground control compared the two theorem statements character-for-character." "`git show` deleted no theorem or lemma line." "The transplanted construction compiled on the first attempt." "The target declaration was re-elaborated independently from a scratch copy and contained no `sorryAx`."], :caution-memory-used "e-codexpilot-bound-the-interface-adapter-heuristic-with-genuine-construction-cases", :classification "The transplant is reusable proof construction, not evidence that the target is merely an interface adapter: it retains topology, polynomial properness, maximum/minimum-modulus reasoning, radial path connectedness, and a finite injection."}, :component-representation {:purpose "Move from quotient-valued `ConnectedComponents` to ambient subsets on which frontier, boundedness, and modulus arguments can be applied.", :properties ["nonempty" "contained in the lemniscate complement" "connected" "open" "frontier contained in the lemniscate"]}}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T18:57:07.043504216Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-cou