{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-derive-a-circle-submean-bound-from-the-circle-average-identity", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "When Mathlib supplies a circle-average identity but the goal is an inequality of norms, rewrite by the identity first and then apply the norm-of-integral bound under the normalized circle parameterization.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Extract the circle-level sub-mean inequality needed before converting a holomorphic estimate to a disk-area estimate.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "derive-a-circle-submean-bound-from-the-circle-average-identity", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "When Mathlib supplies a circle-average identity but the goal is an inequality of norms, rewrite by the identity first and then apply the norm-of-integral bound under the normalized circle parameterization.", :body {:hook "Package closed-ball holomorphicity as `DiffContOnCl`, rewrite the centre value as its circle average, and move the norm through the interval integral to obtain the circle sub-mean inequality.", :capture-kind :runner-axiom-clean-helper-and-ground-control-verification, :problem-class "Extract the circle-level sub-mean inequality needed before converting a holomorphic estimate to a disk-area estimate.", :key-api ["DiffContOnCl.circleAverage" "Real.circleAverage_def" "intervalIntegral.norm_integral_le_integral_norm" "closure_ball" "ball_subset_closedBall"], :witness {:declaration "ApmCanaries.A01A07.norm_le_circleAverage_norm", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false}, :relation-to-existing [{:memory-id "e-codexpilot-package-closed-ball-holomorphicity-as-DiffContOnCl-for-Cauchy-estimates", :shared-interface "Both adapt differentiability on a closed ball to `DiffContOnCl` on the corresponding open ball.", :new-content "The prior memory applies a Cauchy derivative estimate; this record applies the circle-average identity and norm-of-integral inequality."} {:memory-id "e-codexpilot-derive-circle-curve-length-from-the-average-of-the-derivative", :shared-interface "`DiffContOnCl.circleAverage`", :new-content "The prior memory lower-bounds curve length through the average of `f'`; this record upper-bounds a centre value through the average of `‖g‖`."}], :rule "When Mathlib supplies a circle-average identity but the goal is an inequality of norms, rewrite by the identity first and then apply the norm-of-integral bound under the normalized circle parameterization.", :boundary "This is only the circle-level inequality. The disk-area inequality still requires polar coordinates, radial integration, translation invariance, and Fubini.", :result "`‖g z₀‖ ≤ Real.circleAverage (fun w ↦ ‖g w‖) z₀ r`", :how-to-apply ["From `DifferentiableOn ℂ g (closedBall z₀ r)` and `0 < r`, build `DiffContOnCl ℂ g (ball z₀ r)` using restriction to the open ball and continuity on its closure." "Use `DiffContOnCl.circleAverage` to rewrite `g z₀` as `Real.circleAverage g z₀ r`." "Unfold `Real.circleAverage_def` and normalize the positive `2π` scalar." "Apply `intervalIntegral.norm_integral_le_integral_norm` to compare the norm of the complex circle integral with the circle average of `‖g‖`."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T22:19:02.392598002Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-derive-a-circle-submean-bound-from-the-circle-average-identity"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-derive-a-second-order-Schwarz-bound-by-integrating-the-derivative-radially", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "When a holomorphic function and its first derivative vanish at the origin, apply first-order Schwarz rigidity to the derivative and recover the sharper function bound by radial integration.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "derive-a-second-order-Schwarz-bound-by-integrating-the-derivative-radially", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "When a holomorphic function and its first derivative vanish at the origin, apply first-order Schwarz rigidity to the derivative and recover the sharper function bound by radial integration.", :body {:boundary "This yields the stated second-order estimate under a unit bound on `f'`; it is not a general coefficient estimate for arbitrary higher vanishing order.", :capture-kind :runner-Schwarz-plus-radial-integration-construction, :rule "When a holomorphic function and its first derivative vanish at the origin, apply first-order Schwarz rigidity to the derivative and recover the sharper function bound by radial integration.", :key-api ["norm_le_norm_of_mapsTo_ball" "DifferentiableOn.deriv" "norm_sub_le_integral_of_norm_deriv_le_of_le" "integral_id"], :witness {:sorryax false, :commit "b5c01ab", :declarations ["deriv_norm_le_norm" "schwarz_second_order_bound"], :statement-integrity :intact, :all-file-declarations 2}, :hook "Apply Schwarz to `f'` to obtain `‖f'(w)‖≤‖w‖`, then integrate the derivative of `t↦f(tz)` along the radial segment; the exact integral of `t` supplies the factor `1/2`.", :how-to-apply ["Use holomorphicity of `f` and the bound on `f'` to apply the classical Schwarz lemma to `f'`, using `f'(0)=0`." "Fix `z` in the unit disk and define the real path `g(t)=f((t:ℂ)z)` for `t∈[0,1]`." "Compute `g'(t)=z*f'((t:ℂ)z)` by the chain rule." "Combine `‖f'(tz)‖≤‖tz‖` with norm multiplicativity to obtain 