{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-derive-improper-integrability-from-a-monotone-antiderivative-limit", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "When evaluating a nonnegative improper integral, prefer an FTC theorem that derives integrability from a finite antiderivative limit over a route that first assumes or separately reconstructs Bochner integrability.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "derive-improper-integrability-from-a-monotone-antiderivative-limit", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "When evaluating a nonnegative improper integral, prefer an FTC theorem that derives integrability from a finite antiderivative limit over a route that first assumes or separately reconstructs Bochner integrability.", :body {:boundary "The interface requires a nonnegative derivative on the half-line and a finite antiderivative limit; sign-changing or conditionally convergent integrals need a different improper-integral formulation.", :capture-kind :runner-lemma-location-and-owner-full-file-axiom-verification, :rule "When evaluating a nonnegative improper integral, prefer an FTC theorem that derives integrability from a finite antiderivative limit over a route that first assumes or separately reconstructs Bochner integrability.", :key-api ["integral_Ioi_of_hasDerivAt_of_nonneg'" "tendsto_inv_atTop_zero" "tendsto_pow_atTop" "Real.continuousAt_log" "Real.tendsto_arctan_atTop"], :witness {:sorryax false, :commit "42acf6dc98894566dfe1924adeafb49f097f8d16", :declarations ["tendsto_G_atTop" "integral_x7_over_1_plus_x12"], :statement-integrity :intact, :all-file-declarations 10}, :contrast "Unlike a theorem that assumes a Bochner integral bound without integrability, this FTC interface proves integrability as an output before identifying the value and is therefore not vulnerable to `integral_undef`.", :hook "For a nonnegative derivative on a half-line, a finite limit of its antiderivative can establish both integrability and the improper-integral value; no prior integrability hypothesis is needed.", :how-to-apply ["Construct an explicit antiderivative `G` and prove `HasDerivAt G f x` on the positive half-line." "Prove the integrand `f` is pointwise nonnegative there." "Calculate the base value `G 0`." "Prove `G → L` at `+∞`; normalize rational logarithm arguments by the highest power, use continuity of `log` at one, and compose the standard arctangent limit when needed." "Apply `integral_Ioi_of_hasDerivAt_of_nonneg'` to obtain the half-line integral and its integrability from the derivative and finite-limit data." "Finish by normalizing `L-G 0` algebraically."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T02:46:18.667072090Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-derive-improper-integrability-from-a-monotone-antiderivative-limit"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-derive-local-L1-from-weak-L2-by-layer-cake-and-optimized-splitting", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For weak-`L²` to local-`L¹`, integrate the distribution function and optimize the split where the finite-set bound and weak tail bound meet.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Given the weak-`L²` distribution bound `μ{|f| > t} ≤ C/t²`, bound the `L¹` norm over a finite-measure set `E`.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "derive-local-L1-from-weak-L2-by-layer-cake-and-optimized-splitting", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For weak-`L²` to local-`L¹`, integrate the distribution function and optimize the split where the finite-set bound and weak tail bound meet.", :body {:problem-class "Given the weak-`L²` distribution bound `μ{|f| > t} ≤ C/t²`, bound the `L¹` norm over a finite-measure set `E`.", :capture-kind :standard-result-component-search-and-commit-witnessed, :rule "For weak-`L²` to local-`L¹`, integrate the distribution function and optimize the split where the finite-set bound and weak tail bound meet.", :key-api ["MeasureTheory.lintegral_eq_lintegral_meas_lt" "integral_Ioi_rpow_of_lt" "integrableOn_Ioi_rpow_of_lt" "MeasureTheory.norm_integral_le_lintegral_norm" "MeasureTheory.ofReal_integral_eq_lintegral_ofReal" "MeasureTheory.integrable_toReal_of_lintegral_ne_top"], :witness {:declaration "weakL2_implies_L1_bound", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :explicit-constant "2 * Real.sqrt C"}, :route ["Use Cavalieri's principle / layer cake under `volume.restrict E`." "Bound the low distribution tail by `μ(E)`." "Bound the high tail by the weak-`L²` hypothesis `C/t²`." "Split the layer-cake integral at `a = sqrt(C) / sqrt(μ(E))`." "Evaluate the improper integral of `t⁻²`; both pieces equal `sqrt(C * μ(E))`." "Return the explicit constant `C₁ = 2 * sqrt(C)`."], :standard-result "Kolmogorov's inequality for weak `L^p`, specialized to `p