{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-derive-real-liminf-lower-semicontinuity-via-Banach-Steinhaus", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For a real-valued liminf theorem on weakly convergent vectors, use Banach--Steinhaus to prove actual uniform norm boundedness before invoking `le_liminf_of_le`; this supplies the required `IsCoboundedUnder` premise without circular reasoning.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Prove `‖x‖ ≤ liminf (fun n => ‖h n‖) atTop` from weak convergence `h n ⇀ x` in a complete real inner-product space.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "derive-real-liminf-lower-semicontinuity-via-Banach-Steinhaus", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For a real-valued liminf theorem on weakly convergent vectors, use Banach--Steinhaus to prove actual uniform norm boundedness before invoking `le_liminf_of_le`; this supplies the required `IsCoboundedUnder` premise without circular reasoning.", :body {:problem-class "Prove `‖x‖ ≤ liminf (fun n => ‖h n‖) atTop` from weak convergence `h n ⇀ x` in a complete real inner-product space.", :boundary "Nonnegativity supplies a lower bound but not the upper bound on eventual lower bounds required by `IsCoboundedUnder`. The proof therefore depends essentially on completeness through Banach--Steinhaus.", :capture-kind :runner-proof-route-and-ground-control-axiom-verification, :rule "For a real-valued liminf theorem on weakly convergent vectors, use Banach--Steinhaus to prove actual uniform norm boundedness before invoking `le_liminf_of_le`; this supplies the required `IsCoboundedUnder` premise without circular reasoning.", :key-api ["banach_steinhaus" "Metric.isBounded_range_of_tendsto" "innerSL_apply_norm" "isCoboundedUnder_ge_of_eventually_le" "Filter.le_liminf_of_le"], :witness {:declaration "norm_le_liminf_of_weak", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-repair "`[CompleteSpace H]`", :repair-load-bearing true}, :uniform-boundedness ["Represent each `h n` by the continuous linear functional `innerSL ℝ (h n)`." "For each fixed test vector `k`, weak convergence makes `innerSL ℝ (h n) k` converge, hence its range is metrically bounded." "Apply `banach_steinhaus` to obtain one `C` with `‖innerSL ℝ (h n)‖ ≤ C` for every `n`." "Rewrite with `innerSL_apply_norm` to obtain the uniform norm bound `‖h n‖ ≤ C`."], :liminf-bridge ["Turn the uniform upper bound into `IsCoboundedUnder (· ≥ ·) atTop (fun n => ‖h n‖)` using `isCoboundedUnder_ge_of_eventually_le`." "For each `a < ‖x‖`, choose `b = (a + ‖x‖)/2`." "The weak-convergence helper supplies `∀ᶠ n, b ≤ ‖h n‖`." "Apply `le_liminf_of_le` with the coboundedness witness to get `b ≤ liminf ‖h n‖`, and conclude `a < liminf ‖h n‖`." "Finish with `le_of_forall_lt`."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T15:22:06.943606983Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-derive-real-liminf-lower-semicontinuity-via-Banach-Steinhaus"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-derive-the-unit-ball-volume-recursion-through-Wallis-parity-formulas", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For Euclidean ball recursions obtained by slicing, use a trigonometric substitution to expose a Wallis integral, then align parity-specific integral identities with parity-specific exact volume declarations.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Prove the unit Euclidean ball-volume recursion by integrating one-dimensional slices.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "derive-the-unit-ball-volume-recursion-through-Wallis-parity-formulas", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For Euclidean ball recursions obtained by slicing, use a trigonometric substitution to expose a Wallis integral, then align parity-specific integral identities with parity-specific exact volume declarations.", :body {:hook "Turn the one-coordinate ball slice into `∫₀^π sin^(n+1)` with `t = -cos x`, then split the dimension parity so Wallis double-factorial identities meet Mathlib's exact even/odd Euclidean ball-volume formulas.", :capture-kind :runner-proof-ground-control-axiom-verification-and-literature-api-anchor, :problem-class "Prove the unit Euclidean ball-volume recursion by integrating one-dimensional slices.", :key-api ["intervalIntegral.integral_comp_mul_deriv" "integral_sin_pow_even" "integral_sin_pow_odd" "InnerProductSpace.volume_ball_of_dim_even" "InnerProductSpace.volume_ball_of_dim_odd" "Nat.doubleFactorial_eq_prod_even" "Nat.doubleFactorial_eq_prod_odd" "Nat.doubleFactorial_two_mul" "Nat.even_or_odd'"], :witness {:declaration "ApmCanaries.A01A04.ball_volume_recursion", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-integrity :intact}, :proof-shape {:slice "∫ t, ballSlice(t)^n = ∫ x in 0..π, sin(x)^(n+1)", :parity "Even and odd `n` select complementary exact ball-volume and Wallis formulas.", :normalization "Factorial and double-factorial identities reduce both branches to field arithmetic."}, :rule "For Euclidean ball recursions obtained by slicing, use a trigonometric substitution to expose a Wallis integral, then align parity-specific integral identities with parity-specific exact volume declarations.", :boundary "The route depends on the Euclidean norm and the installed exact ball-volume API; it does not apply unchanged to the earlier sup-norm statement that was repaired in this file.", :literature-anchor {:use-status :api-pointer-used, :contribution "The thread identified PR #19949 as adding the exact even/odd Euclidean ball-volume formulas that enabled the parity route.", :source "leanprover-community Zulip archive", :thread "Roadmap to high school geometry"}, :route-improvement {:classification :confirming-instance, :existing-memory-id "e-codexpilot-override-a-documented-proof-route-when-component-evidence-favors-another", :observation "The inherited route was followed through slicing and Wallis, but its proposed manual Gamma-recurrence reconciliation was replaced by the installed exact even/odd ball-volume API.", :boundary "This confirms the existing route-override rule; it does not establish that Gamma-based proofs are generally inferior."}, :formalization-arcs ["Normalize the derivative of `-cos` explicitly: `-(-sin x)` must be simplified to `sin x` before the substitution theorem matches." "Supply continuity and interval-integrability facts explicitly around `intervalIntegral.integral_comp_mul_deriv`." "Watch rewrite orientation for `Finset.prod_div_distrib`; the Wallis products and double-factorial products may face opposite directions." "Use `omega` to normalize the parity indices before rewriting the exact volume formulas."], :how-to-apply ["Express the slice kernel as `sqrt (1-t²)` on `[-1,1]` and zero outside; rewrite the whole-line integral as an interval integral using an indicator." "Apply the interval substitution `t = -cos x` on `[0,π]`; its derivative contributes one additional sine factor, yielding `∫₀^π sin x^(n+1)`." "Rewrite Mathlib's `integral_sin_pow_even` and `integral_sin_pow_odd` product formulas into double-factorial form." "Split `n` with `Nat.even_or_odd'` so that the two adjacent ball dimensions match `InnerProductSpace.volume_ball_of_dim_even` and `InnerProductSpace.volume_ball_of_dim_odd`." "Use `Nat.doubleFactorial_two_mul`, factorial nonzeroness, and field normalization to close each parity branch." "Prefer the exact parity-specific volume API over manually reconciling a Gamma recurrence when those declarations are available in the installed Mathlib revision."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T21:32:10.217582060Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-derive-the-unit-ball-volume-recursion-through-Wallis-parity-formulas"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-descend-an-even-analytic-function-through-the-squaring-map", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For descent through a branched map, split the proof at the branch locus: reindex the invariant Taylor germ where the derivative vanishes, and use the analytic inverse-function theorem everywhere else.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Construct an analytic factor `g` for an even analytic function `h`, with `h z = g (z²)`, across the branch point at zero.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "descend-an-even-analytic-function-through-the-squaring-map", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For descent through a branched map, split the proof at the branch locus: reindex the invariant Taylor germ where the derivative vanishes, and use the analytic inverse-function theorem everywhere else.", :body {:problem-class "Construct an analytic factor `g` for an even analytic function `h`, with `h z = g (z²)`, across the branch point at zero.", :boundary "Evenness is load-bearing for independence from the two square-root choices and for annihilating odd Taylor coefficients. The inverse-function step cannot cover zero because the derivative of `z ↦ z²` vanishes there.", :capture-kind :runner-multi-step-construction-and-ground-control-verification, :rule "For descent through a branched map, split the proof at the branch locus: reindex the invariant Taylor germ where the derivative vanishes, and use the analytic inverse-function theorem everywhere else.", :key-api ["FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars" "FormalMultilinearSeries.le_mul_pow_of_radius_pos" "FormalMultilinearSeries.le_radius_of_bound" "HasFPowerSeriesAt.eventually_hasSum" "tsum_even_add_odd" "analyticAt_comp_iff_of_deriv_ne_zero"], :witness {:declaration "apm_a96J10_even_factors", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-integrity :intact, :helpers ["evenFactorRoot" "evenFactorRoot_sq" "evenFactorRoot_tendsto" "evenCoefficients_radius_pos" "evenCoefficients_sum"]}, :construction ["Choose a square root only to define the pointwise factor; the selector itself need not be analytic because evenness makes the value independent of the sign." "At zero, expand `h` as a formal power series, use vanishing of all odd coefficients, and reindex the even coefficients into a new series." "Prove the reindexed series has positive radius using coefficient bounds inherited from the original series." "Use `tsum_even_add_odd` and the zero odd part to identify the new series after composition with `z ↦ z²`." "At a nonzero point, the derivative of the squaring map is nonzero; use `analyticAt_comp_iff_of_deriv_ne_zero` to descend analyticity through its local inverse." "Combine the Taylor-germ argument at the branch point with the inverse-function argument away from it."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T18:18:48.223488211Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-descend-an-even-analytic-function-through-the-squaring-map"}}
