{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-evaluate-a-boundary-series-by-alternating-convergence-Abel-and-a-closed-form", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For a classical series at the boundary of a power-series disk, separate three jobs: establish convergence without knowing the value, use Abel to move the unknown sum to a radial limit, and evaluate that radial limit through an interior closed form.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Evaluate a conditionally convergent boundary series when its associated power series has a known closed form only inside the open radius of convergence.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "evaluate-a-boundary-series-by-alternating-convergence-Abel-and-a-closed-form", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For a classical series at the boundary of a power-series disk, separate three jobs: establish convergence without knowing the value, use Abel to move the unknown sum to a radial limit, and evaluate that radial limit through an interior closed form.", :body {:capture-kind :runner-composed-route-zulip-anchor-and-ground-control-axiom-verification, :problem-class "Evaluate a conditionally convergent boundary series when its associated power series has a known closed form only inside the open radius of convergence.", :key-api ["tendsto_alternating_series_of_tendsto_zero" "tendsto_tsum_powerSeries_nhdsWithin_lt" "hasSum_pow_div_log_of_abs_lt_one" "HasSum.congr_fun" "tendsto_nhds_unique"], :witness {:axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :declarations ["tendsto_sum_alternating_harmonic" "alternating_harmonic_eq_log_two"], :statement-integrity :intact}, :rule "For a classical series at the boundary of a power-series disk, separate three jobs: establish convergence without knowing the value, use Abel to move the unknown sum to a radial limit, and evaluate that radial limit through an interior closed form.", :boundary "The alternating-series test alone supplies no value, while the interior Taylor identity alone does not justify substitution at the boundary. Abel's theorem is the necessary bridge between them.", :literature-anchor {:kind :zulip-formalization-precedent, :path "217875-Is-there-code-for-X%3F/Bounds.20on.20alternating.20convergent.20series.json", :use-status :route-supplied, :contribution "The thread explicitly combines an alternating-series theorem, a Taylor series, and Abel's theorem and records development of Mathlib's real Abel theorem."}, :formalization-arcs ["Convert the Mercator `HasSum` term-by-term to the shifted alternating-harmonic coefficients with `HasSum.congr_fun`." "Multiply the Abel limit by `x`, whose one-sided limit is one, so the radial expression becomes `log (1+x)` near the boundary." "Compare the resulting limit with continuity of `log (1+x)` at `x = 1` and use `tendsto_nhds_unique`."], :composition [{:stage :existence, :standard-result "Alternating series test", :work "Use `tendsto_alternating_series_of_tendsto_zero` to prove convergence of the boundary series to an initially unknown limit `l`."} {:stage :boundary-identification, :standard-result "Abel's limit theorem", :work "Apply `tendsto_tsum_powerSeries_nhdsWithin_lt` to identify `l` with the one-sided radial limit of the associated power series as `x → 1⁻`."} {:stage :evaluation, :standard-result "Mercator logarithm series", :work "Use `hasSum_pow_div_log_of_abs_lt_one` to prove that the radial power series equals `log (1+x)/x` for `0 < x < 1`, then take the one-sided limit to obtain `log 2`."}]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T15:42:30.764802518Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loo