{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-evaluate-a-rational-circle-integral-by-separating-interior-and-exterior-poles", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For a rational unit-circle integral with separated simple poles, classify poles geometrically before performing algebra; the inside/outside split determines whether Cauchy's formula or Cauchy–Goursat supplies each term.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "evaluate-a-rational-circle-integral-by-separating-interior-and-exterior-poles", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For a rational unit-circle integral with separated simple poles, classify poles geometrically before performing algebra; the inside/outside split determines whether Cauchy's formula or Cauchy–Goursat supplies each term.", :body {:boundary "The method assumes no pole lies on the contour and that the denominator factors into poles whose disk membership can be proved.", :capture-kind :runner-contour-construction-and-owner-full-file-verification, :rule "For a rational unit-circle integral with separated simple poles, classify poles geometrically before performing algebra; the inside/outside split determines whether Cauchy's formula or Cauchy–Goursat supplies each term.", :key-api ["circleIntegral.integral_sub_inv_of_mem_ball" "circleIntegral_eq_zero_of_differentiable_on_off_countable" "circleIntegral.integral_const_mul" "circleIntegral.integral_sub" "circleIntegral" "intervalIntegral.integral_congr"], :witness {:sorryax false, :commit "146de41665ed60d3e0a5a43709e194e50c9c9e0d", :declarations ["contour_integral_eval" "integral_inv_two_plus_cos"], :statement-integrity :intact, :all-file-declarations 7}, :hook "Factor the denominator, split it into simple poles, evaluate the pole inside the circle by Cauchy's formula, and kill the exterior pole by Cauchy–Goursat before returning to the real angular integral.", :how-to-apply ["Factor the quadratic denominator and prove which root lies inside and which lies outside the unit circle." "Establish a partial-fraction identity away from both roots." "Use the circle Cauchy integral formula for the interior simple pole." "Show the exterior-pole integrand is differentiable on the closed disk and apply the zero contour-integral theorem." "Combine the two contour values algebraically." "Unfold `circleIntegral`, prove the pointwise identity under `z=exp(iθ)`, and transfer equality through `intervalIntegral.integral_congr`."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T02:10:56.188829900Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-evaluate-a-rational-circle-integral-by-separating-interior-and-exterior-poles"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-evaluate-the-Dirichlet-sinc-integral-by-Abel-regularization-and-uniform-tails", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "To remove Abel damping from a conditionally convergent integral, combine a damping-independent tail estimate with ordinary dominated convergence on a fixed compact head; neither ingredient alone controls the improper limit.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Evaluate a conditionally convergent improper oscillatory integral when Mathlib has neither the final sinc theorem nor a directly packaged Abel theorem.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "evaluate-the-Dirichlet-sinc-integral-by-Abel-regularization-and-uniform-tails", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "To remove Abel damping from a conditionally convergent integral, combine a damping-independent tail estimate with ordinary dominated convergence on a fixed compact head; neither ingredient alone controls the improper limit.", :body {:hook "Evaluate the exponentially damped sinc integral as `arctan(1/a)`, then combine fixed-interval damping removal with a uniform Dirichlet tail bound to identify the undamped limit as `π/2`.", :capture-kind :three-attempt-frontier-memory-compounding-and-ground-control-full-file-verification, :problem-class "Evaluate a conditionally convergent improper oscillatory integral when Mathlib has neither the final sinc theorem nor a directly packaged Abel theorem.", :key-api ["cauchy_map_iff_exists_tendsto" "intervalIntegral_integral_swap" "integral_div_sq_add_sq" "intervalIntegral.integral_mul_deriv_eq_deriv_mul" "intervalIntegral_tendsto_integral_Ioi" "tendsto_integral_filter_of_dominated_convergence" "tendsto_nhds_unique" "Real.arctan_inv_of_pos" "Real.sinc_neg"], :witness {:declaration "dirichlet_integral_improper", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :all-file-declarations 17, :added-declarations 11}, :rule "To remove Abel damping from a conditionally convergent integral, combine a damping-independent tail estimate with ordinary dominated convergence on a fixed compact head; neither ingredient alone controls the improper limit.", :negative-search-cache {:reused true, :mathlib "Sinc and ImproperIntegrals contained no final sinc evaluation or directly applicable Abel theorem.", :zulip "No formalized Dirichlet-integral construction was found.", :arxiv "The previously checked sinc papers were background only and supplied no construction anchor.", :effect "Attempts 2 and 3 did not rerun Zulip or arXiv; they continued from the recorded construction frontier."}, :frontier-provenance {:used-memories ["e-codexpilot-derive-a-sinc-tail-identity-by-differentiating-cosine-over-x" "e-codexpilot-remove-Abel-regularization-from-the-Dirichlet-sinc-integral"], :history "Both memories were drafted from the first blocked run, used to establish convergence in attempt 2, and used again to finish the numerical identification in attempt 3."}, :boundary "The direct Bochner integral of `sinc` over all of `ℝ` is not the target: conditional convergence must be stated as a `Tendsto` limit of bounded-interval integrals.", :proof-phases [{:phase :undamped-convergence, :result "`∫₀ᴿ sinc → L` for some `L`", :engine "Dirichlet tail/Cauchy criterion"} {:phase :damped-evaluation, :result "`∫₀∞ exp(-a*x)*sinc x = arctan(1/a)`", :engine "parameter integral, Fubini, Laplace transform of cosine"} {:phase :uniform-removal, :result "damped integral tends to the same `L` as `a → 0+`", :engine "uniform Dirichlet tail plus fixed-interval dominated convergence"} {:phase :identification, :result "`L = π/2`, symmetric limit `π`", :engine "arctangent limit, uniqueness, evenness"}], :how-to-apply ["First prove convergence of the undamped positive-half-line integrals from the integration-by-parts tail estimate `|∫_A^B sinc| ≤ 2/A`." "Represent `sinc x` as `∫₀¹ cos(t*x) dt`." "For `a > 0`, prove product integrability and use Fubini to evaluate `∫₀∞ exp(-a*x)*sinc x dx` as `∫₀¹ a/(a²+t²) dt = arctan(1/a)`." "Apply Abel summation to the primitive of `sinc` and obtain a damped tail bound uniform in `a`, here `|∫_A^B exp(-a*x)*sinc x dx| ≤ 4/A`." "Pass the finite damped tail estimate to the improper tail." "On a fixed interval `[0,A]`, remove the damping by dominated convergence as `a → 0+`." "Use a three-error decomposition: undamped head near its limit, damped head near the undamped head, and uniformly small damped tail." "Compare the resulting damped limit with `arctan(1/a) → π/2` and use uniqueness of limits." "Use evenness of `Real.sinc` to double the positive-half-line limit and obtain the symmetric value `π`."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T00:10:52.559054349Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-evaluate-the-Dirichlet-sinc-integral-by-Abel-regularization-and-uniform-tails"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-exclude-the-real-unit-segment-from-a-principal-fourth-root-image", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "To exclude a real interval from a principal-root image, assume interval membership and push it back through the exact power identity; real/imaginary projections often expose the contradiction more cleanly than branch-argument inequalities.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Exclude a deleted real segment from the image of a branch-sensitive complex root when argument bounds alone only prove wedge membership.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "exclude-the-real-unit-segment-from-a-principal-fourth-root-image", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "To exclude a real interval from a principal-root image, assume interval membership and push it back through the exact power identity; real/imaginary projections often expose the contradiction more cleanly than branch-argument inequalities.", :body {:problem-class "Exclude a deleted real segment from the image of a branch-sensitive complex root when argument bounds alone only prove wedge membership.", :boundary "The argument needs a valid root-power identity at the chosen branch and a source invariant strong enough to contradict the pulled-back real interval.", :capture-kind :runner-branch-cut-helper-and-ground-control-verification, :rule "To exclude a real interval from a principal-root image, assume interval membership and push it back through the exact power identity; real/imaginary projections often expose the contradiction more cleanly than branch-argument inequalities.", :witness {:declaration "fourthRoot_not_mem_unitSegment", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false}, :hook "If the principal fourth root were a real `q ∈ [0,1]`, raising it to the fourth power would force the source `η` to be real with `0 ≤ η.re ≤ 1`, contradicting the slit-plane invariant.", :how-to-apply ["Assume `η^(1/4)` has zero imaginary part and real part `q` in `[0,1]`." "Use the principal-power identity `(η^(1/4))^4 = η` under the established nonzero/branch hypotheses." "Project the equality to real and imaginary parts." "Show `η.im = 0` and `η.re = q^4 ≤ 1`." "Contradict the incoming disjunction `1 < η.re ∨ η.im ≠ 0`."], :key-move "Pull segment membership back through a finite power identity instead of trying to reason directly about the principal root's argument at the boundary."}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :arc-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T00:10:50.332383709Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-exclude-the-real-unit-segment-from-a-principal-fourth-root-image"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-extend-a-reciprocal-across-finite-punctures-then-apply-Liouville", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "When a holomorphic function blows up at finitely many punctures and infinity, invert an omitted-value translate: zero-fill the reciprocal, remove the singularities, and let Liouville turn decay at infinity into a contradiction.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Show that a holomorphic function on the complement of a finite set, blowing up at every puncture and at infinity, cannot omit a complex value.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "extend-a-reciprocal-across-finite-punctures-then-apply-Liouville", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "When a holomorphic function blows up at finitely many punctures and infinity, invert an omitted-value translate: zero-fill the reciprocal, remove the singularities, and let Liouville turn decay at infinity into a contradiction.", :body {:problem-class "Show that a holomorphic function on the complement of a finite set, blowing up at every puncture and at infinity, cannot omit a complex value.", :capture-kind :runner-classical-route-and-ground-control-verification, :rule "When a holomorphic function blows up at finitely many punctures and infinity, invert an omitted-value translate: zero-fill the reciprocal, remove the singularities, and let Liouville turn decay at infinity into a contradiction.", :key-api ["Complex.analyticAt_of_differentiable_on_punctured_nhds_of_continuousAt" "continuousAt_iff_punctured_nhds" "Filter.EventuallyEq.differentiableAt_iff" "Differentiable.eq_const_of_tendsto_cocompact" "Finset.isClosed"], :witness {:declaration "analytic_blowup_surjective", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-integrity :intact}, :route ["Assume a value `w₀` is omitted and form `(f - w₀)⁻¹` off the finite puncture set `F`." "Extend the reciprocal by zero at every point of `F`." "Use the given blow-up limit to prove the extension is continuous at each puncture." "Apply `Complex.analyticAt_of_differentiable_on_punctured_nhds_of_continuousAt` at every puncture; off `F`, transfer differentiability from the reciprocal by eventual equality." "Convert the reciprocal's norm tending to zero at infinity into convergence of the extension to zero along `cocompact ℂ`." "Apply `Differentiable.eq_const_of_tendsto_cocompact`; the entire extension is identically zero." "Choose a point outside the finite set. There the extension is a reciprocal of a nonzero value and hence nonzero, contradicting constancy."], :standard-results ["Riemann removable singularity theorem" "Liouville's theorem"]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T14:48:10.645671177Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-extend-a-reciprocal-across-finite-punctures-then-apply-Liouville"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-extend-eLpNorm-to-essential-supremum-from-probability-to-finite-measure", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "To generalize the probability-space `Lᵖ → L∞` proof to a finite measure, retain the superlevel lower bound but replace probability monotonicity by explicit measure factors; prove every nonzero finite factor `m^(1/p)` tends to one and split off the zero measure.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "extend-eLpNorm-to-essential-supremum-from-probability-to-finite-measure", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "To generalize the probability-space `Lᵖ → L∞` proof to a finite measure, retain the superlevel lower bound but replace probability monotonicity by explicit measure factors; prove every nonzero finite factor `m^(1/p)` tends to one and split off the zero measure.", :body {:capture-kind :runner-finite-measure-generalization-and-ground-control-axiom-verification, :key-api ["Filter.Tendsto.nnrpow" "eLpNorm_le_eLpNorm_mul_rpow_measure_univ" "eLpNorm_indicator_const₀" "eLpNorm_mono_enorm" "eLpNorm_exponent_top" "eLpNormEssSup" "essSup_le_of_ae_le" "tendsto_order"], :witness {:declaration "tendsto_eLpNorm_atTop", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-integrity :intact, :helper "tendsto_measure_rpow_one_div"}, :relation-to-existing {:memory-id "e-codexpilot-prove-eLpNorm-to-essential-supremum-by-superlevel-and-probability-monotonicity", :shared-content "The positive-measure superlevel-set argument supplies the lower bound in both proofs.", :new-content "Without a probability measure, exponent monotonicity does not give the required upper bound directly. The finite-measure proof tracks `μ(univ)^(1/p)` and superlevel-measure factors explicitly, proves both tend to one, and handles `μ = 0` separately."}, :rule "To generalize the probability-space `Lᵖ → L∞` proof to a finite measure, retain the superlevel lower bound but replace probability monotonicity by explicit measure factors; prove every nonzero finite factor `m^(1/p)` tends to one and split off the zero measure.", :lower-bound ["For `a < eLpNorm f ⊤ μ`, choose `a < b < eLpNorm f ⊤ μ`." "Let `s = {x | b < ‖f x‖ₑ}`." "Show `μ s ≠ 0`: otherwise `essSup_le_of_ae_le` would force `eLpNorm f ⊤ μ ≤ b`." "Compare the indicator constant on `s` with `f` to obtain `b * μ(s)^(1/p) ≤ eLpNorm f p μ`." "Use the scalar limit for `μ s` to make this lower bound eventually exceed `a`."], :scope {:language :lean4, :problem "Prove `eLpNorm f p μ → eLpNorm f ⊤ μ` as `p → ∞` for a bounded a.e.-strongly-measurable function on an arbitrary finite measure space."}, :boundary "Finiteness of `μ(univ)` is load-bearing for the upper factor and for finiteness of superlevel measures. The proof does not extend unchanged to an infinite measure space.", :upper-bound ["Apply `eLpNorm_le_eLpNorm_mul_rpow_measure_univ` with endpoint exponent `⊤`." "This gives `eLpNorm f p μ ≤ eLpNorm f ⊤ μ * μ(univ)^(1/p)`." "Use the scalar limit for `μ(univ)` to make the upper comparison converge to `eLpNorm f ⊤ μ`."], :assembly "Handle `μ = 0` by simplification; otherwise combine the eventual lower and upper bounds with `tendsto_order`.", :scalar-limit ["For nonzero finite `m : ℝ≥0∞`, prove `m^(1/p) → 1` as `p → ∞`." "Show the real exponent tends to zero." "Pass to `m.toNNReal`, use `Filter.Tendsto.nnrpow`, and transport the limit back through the ENNReal coercion." "Record the required side conditions `m ≠ 0` and `m ≠ ⊤`; these are why the zero-measure case is split off."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T15:57:10.896223343Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {