{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-extend-weak-convergence-from-a-dense-linear-span-by-uniform-boundedness", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For weak convergence of a uniformly bounded sequence, prove convergence on generators, close under finite linear combinations, extend by a uniform norm bound to the closed span, and remove the orthogonal complement by projection.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Prove `⟪g, f_m⟫ → 0` for every vector `g` from pairwise decay of a unit-vector sequence.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "extend-weak-convergence-from-a-dense-linear-span-by-uniform-boundedness", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For weak convergence of a uniformly bounded sequence, prove convergence on generators, close under finite linear combinations, extend by a uniform norm bound to the closed span, and remove the orthogonal complement by projection.", :body {:problem-class "Prove `⟪g, f_m⟫ → 0` for every vector `g` from pairwise decay of a unit-vector sequence.", :capture-kind :runner-proof-route-and-ground-control-verification, :rule "For weak convergence of a uniformly bounded sequence, prove convergence on generators, close under finite linear combinations, extend by a uniform norm bound to the closed span, and remove the orthogonal complement by projection.", :key-api ["Submodule.span_induction" "Metric.mem_closure_iff" "Submodule.topologicalClosure_coe" "norm_inner_le_norm" "Submodule.inner_orthogonalProjection_eq_of_mem_right"], :witness {:declaration "inner_tendsto_zero", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false}, :route ["For a fixed generator `f_n`, use the pairwise decay hypothesis once `m > n`." "Extend convergence from generators to their algebraic span with `Submodule.span_induction` and linearity of the inner product." "Extend from the span to its topological closure: approximate a target vector within `ε/2`, use `‖f_m‖ = 1`, and bound the approximation error by Cauchy–Schwarz via `norm_inner_le_norm`." "Orthogonally project an arbitrary `g` onto the closed span." "Use `Submodule.inner_orthogonalProjection_eq_of_mem_right` to discard the orthogonal component, whose pairing with every `f_m` is zero."], :lean-arcs ["Induct on the span-membership proof itself." "For closure membership, unfold `Submodule.topologicalClosure_coe` and use `subset_closure`." "Normalize the real inner-product norm with `Real.norm_eq_abs` before the `ε/2` estimate."], :standard-result "A uniformly bounded sequence converges weakly to zero when its pairings converge to zero on a dense linear subspace."}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T14:04:21.527825188Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-extend-weak-convergence-from-a-dense-linear-span-by-uniform-boundedness"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-force-a-sublinear-entire-function-constant-by-Cauchy-derivative-estimates", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For an entire function with sublinear polynomial growth, replace bounded Liouville by Cauchy's derivative estimate at an expanding radius; removable quotients can manufacture the needed sublinear entire function.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "force-a-sublinear-entire-function-constant-by-Cauchy-derivative-estimates", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For an entire function with sublinear polynomial growth, replace bounded Liouville by Cauchy's derivative estimate at an expanding radius; removable quotients can manufacture the needed sublinear entire function.", :body {:boundary "The quotient must extend holomorphically across its apparent singularity, and the growth exponent must be strictly below one for the first-derivative bound to vanish at infinity.", :capture-kind :runner-removable-quotient-and-sublinear-Liouville-construction, :rule "For an entire function with sublinear polynomial growth, replace bounded Liouville by Cauchy's derivative estimate at an expanding radius; removable quotients can manufacture the needed sublinear entire function.", :key-api ["Complex.analyticAt_of_differentiable_on_punctured_nhds_of_continuousAt" "Complex.norm_deriv_le_of_forall_mem_sphere_norm_le" "is_const_of_deriv_eq_zero"], :witness {:sorryax false, :commit "662b9ec", :declarations ["quadraticQuotient_continuousAt_zero" "quadraticQuotient_differentiable" "eq_const_of_norm_le_rpow_half" "no_entire_lower_bound_three_halves"], :statement-integrity :intact, :all-file-declarations 9}, :hook "If a removable quotient grows only like `‖z‖^(1/2)`, apply Cauchy's derivative estimate on circles of arbitrarily large radius; the derivative bound tends to zero even though ordinary bounded Liouville does not apply.", :how-to-apply ["From the lower bound on `f`, first prove `f z ≠ 0` away from the origin." "Define `q z = 0` at the origin and `q z = z²/f z` elsewhere." "Use the lower bound to prove `‖q z‖ ≤ ‖z‖^(1/2)` and hence continuity at zero." "Combine differentiability on the punctured neighbourhood with continuity at zero via the removable-singularity theorem to make `q` entire." "Apply the Cauchy derivative estimate to `q` on a circle of radius `R`; the growth bound gives `‖q'(z)‖ ≤ R^(1/2)/R` up to the fixed-centre adjustment." "Let `R→∞` to force every derivative to zero, then use derivative-zero constancy." "Evaluate the constant quotient at selected points to contradict the original nonvanishing lower bound."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T03:16:19.593901042Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-force-a-sublinear-entire-function-constant-by-Cauchy-derivative-estimates"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-frontier-of-open-connected-component-lies-in-ambient-frontier", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "Relate the ambient frontier of `connectedComponentIn U x` to the frontier of an open ambient subset `U` in a locally connected space.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Relate the ambient frontier of `connectedComponentIn U x` to the frontier of an open ambient subset `U` in a locally connected space.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "frontier-of-open-connected-component-lies-in-ambient-frontier", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "Use `hU.connectedComponentIn` to show the component is open, so its interior is itself. → The component is contained in `U`, hence closure monotonicity supplies the closure half of frontier membership. → Express the relative component as the image of `connectedComponent (⟨x,hx⟩ : U)` using `connectedComponentIn_eq_image hx`. → Use closedness/maximality of the connected component in the subtype to show `U ↓∩ connectedComponentIn U x` is relatively closed. → Transfer relative closedness with `isClosed_preimage_val.mp`; a putative frontier point lying in `U` would then lie back in the component, contradicting the frontier's non-interior half.", :body {:problem-class "Relate the ambient frontier of `connectedComponentIn U x` to the frontier of an open ambient subset `U` in a locally connected space.", :proof-shape ["Use `hU.connectedComponentIn` to show the component is open, so its interior is itself." "The component is contained in `U`, hence closure monotonicity supplies the closure half of frontier membership." "Express the relative component as the image of `connectedComponent (⟨x,hx⟩ : U)` using `connectedComponentIn_eq_image hx`." "Use closedness/maximality of the connected component in the subtype to show `U ↓∩ connectedComponentIn U x` is relatively closed." "Transfer relative closedness with `isClosed_preimage_val.mp`; a putative frontier point lying in `U` would then lie back in the component, contradicting the frontier's non-interior half."], :boundary "This helper closes the ambient-frontier API gap only. It does not prove connectedness of the polynomial superlevel or count sublevel components.", :capture-kind :runner-narrated-and-commit-witnessed, :statement "frontier (connectedComponentIn U x) ⊆ frontier U", :preconditions ["`LocallyConnectedSpace α`" "`IsOpen U`" "`x ∈ U`"], :key-api ["IsOpen.connectedComponentIn" "connectedComponentIn_subset" "connectedComponentIn_eq_image" "isClosed_connectedComponent" "isClosed_preimage_val"], :witness {:declaration "ConstructionTargets.LemniscateComponents.frontier_connectedComponentIn_subset_frontier", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false}}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/cron-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-28T14:53:45.726604440Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-frontier-of-open-connected-component-lies-in-ambient-frontier"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-identify-an-L1-kernel-from-its-action-on-smooth-test-derivatives", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "To identify an `L¹` convolution kernel from its action on test derivatives, subtract the candidate kernel, smooth by convolution, kill the resulting constant using infinite volume, and invoke distributional uniqueness.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Identify an integrable kernel `g` from the identity `g ⋆ f' = f(x+h) - f(x-h)` for every smooth compactly supported test function.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "identify-an-L1-kernel-from-its-action-on-smooth-test-derivatives", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "To identify an `L¹` convolution kernel from its action on test derivatives, subtract the candidate kernel, smooth by convolution, kill the resulting constant using infinite volume, and invoke distributional uniqueness.", :body {:problem-class "Identify an integrable kernel `g` from the identity `g ⋆ f' = f(x+h) - f(x-h)` for every smooth compactly supported test function.", :capture-kind :runner-proof-route-and-ground-control-verification, :rule "To identify an `L¹` convolution kernel from its action on test derivatives, subtract the candidate kernel, smooth by convolution, kill the resulting constant using infinite volume, and invoke distributional uniqueness.", :key-api ["intervalIntegral.integral_deriv_of_contDiffOn_uIcc" "HasCompactSupport.hasDerivAt_convolution_right" "Integrable.integrable_convolution" "is_const_of_deriv_eq_zero" "ae_eq_zero_of_integral_contDiff_smul_eq_zero"], :witness {:declaration "convolution_identity_implies_indicator", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-integrity :intact}, :route ["Let `χ` be the indicator of `[-h,h]` and set `k = g - χ`." "Use the fundamental theorem of calculus to prove `χ ⋆ f' = f(x+h) - f(x-h)`, hence `k ⋆ f' = 0` for every smooth compactly supported `f`." "Given an arbitrary test function `q`, reflect it by defining `f(x) = q(-x)`." "Use convolution smoothing to obtain `(k ⋆ f)' = k ⋆ f' = 0`, then apply derivative-zero constancy." "Prove the constant is zero: `k ⋆ f` is integrable, while a nonzero constant is not integrable over the infinite-volume space `ℝ`." "Evaluate the zero convolution at the origin to obtain `∫ q x • k x = 0`." "Apply `ae_eq_zero_of_integral_contDiff_smul_eq_zero` and unfold `k` and `χ` to conclude `g = χ` almost everywhere."], :standard-results ["fundamental theorem of calculus" "differentiation of convolution" "derivative-zero implies constancy" "fundamental lemma of the calculus of variations / distributional uniqueness"], :infinite-volume-step {:role "This converts derivative-zero constancy into vanishing, rather than merely identifying an unknown additive constant.", :api ["integrable_const_iff" "not_isFiniteMeasure_iff" "Real.volume_univ"]}}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T12:41:32.032345674Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-identify-an-L1-kernel-from-its-action-on-smooth-test-derivatives"}}
