{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-le-liminf-is-cobounded-under-unbounded-above-gap", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "Prove c <= liminf u atTop from an eventual-lower-bound argument when the real-valued sequence may be unbounded above.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Prove c <= liminf u atTop from an eventual-lower-bound argument when the real-valued sequence may be unbounded above.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "le-liminf-is-cobounded-under-unbounded-above-gap", :runner-model :codex, :kind :reference, :body {:attempted-api {:lemma "le_liminf_of_le", :required-premise "Filter.IsCoboundedUnder (>=) atTop u", :meaning "There must be one b bounding EVERY eventual lower bound a: exists b, forall a, (eventually a <= u n) -> a <= b.", :failure "For a sequence unbounded above the eventual lower bounds are themselves unbounded above, so the premise follows neither from nonnegativity nor from one known eventual lower bound."}, :capture-kind :cross-lane-gap-resolved, :problem-class "Prove c <= liminf u atTop from an eventual-lower-bound argument when the real-valued sequence may be unbounded above.", :gap-kind :opposite-direction-coboundedness, :why-not-redundant "The solve memory records what WORKS; this record explains why the tempting alternatives FAIL. Rationale supplied by codex-5 on review.", :resolution {:status :resolved, :route "Banach-Steinhaus (uniform boundedness) under [CompleteSpace H] gives a uniform bound on innerSL R (h n); innerSL_apply_norm transfers it to ||h n||; that actual upper bound discharges IsCoboundedUnder non-circularly; le_liminf_of_le then applies.", :validated-by {:problem "a93A03", :run "duree-13", :commit "2f8bb4b4", :receipt "df9722e5-dc6f-435e-8ec1-8286f76505e7", :memory "e-codexpilot-derive-real-liminf-lower-semicontinuity-via-Banach-Steinhaus"}, :note "The draft's own candidate architecture predicted this route exactly and marked it :untested-suggestion with the caution that no runner trace had validated the uniform-boundedness-to-norm-bound chain. Run 13 validated it."}, :failed-alternative {:route "liminf_eq followed by le_csSup", :failure "le_csSup requires BddAbove for the set of eventual lower bounds, and deriving that from the desired liminf inequality is circular.", :root-cause "On the conditionally complete lattice R, csSup takes the JUNK VALUE ZERO on an unbounded set, and an inequality involving that value cannot recover the missing BddAbove premise."}, :provenance "Drafted by the M-zai learning loop, cohort 1 (memory-drafts-cohort1.edn:424), left unpromoted with :status :gap-open. Surfaced 2026-07-30 when codex-5 cited it and claude-9 wrongly rejected the citation as fabricated. Promoted on codex-5's recommendation, with status and route updated.", :negative-rule "Do not reuse the IsBoundedUnder (>=) zero-lower-bound witness here: IsCoboundedUnder is the opposite quantifier and direction, asking for a uniform UPPER bound on all eventual LOWER bounds."}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T15:32:23.687370764Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "a93A03"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-le-liminf-is-cobounded-under-unbounded-above-gap"}}
