{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-normalize-r3-radial-coefficient-to-four-pi", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "Normalize the general Haar radial coefficient in dimension three to the familiar `4π` factor.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Normalize the general Haar radial coefficient in dimension three to the familiar `4π` factor.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "normalize-r3-radial-coefficient-to-four-pi", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "Rewrite with `MeasureTheory.integral_fun_norm_addHaar (volume : Measure E) g`. → Simplify the Euclidean dimension and scalar actions. → Rewrite the real measure coefficient using `measureReal_def` and `EuclideanSpace.volume_ball_fin_three`. → Supply positivity so the `ENNReal.toReal (ENNReal.ofReal ...)` coefficient reduces. → Commute `r²` and `g r` pointwise, then close the remaining coefficient identity with ring normalization.", :body {:problem-class "Normalize the general Haar radial coefficient in dimension three to the familiar `4π` factor.", :proof-shape ["Rewrite with `MeasureTheory.integral_fun_norm_addHaar (volume : Measure E) g`." "Simplify the Euclidean dimension and scalar actions." "Rewrite the real measure coefficient using `measureReal_def` and `EuclideanSpace.volume_ball_fin_three`." "Supply positivity so the `ENNReal.toReal (ENNReal.ofReal ...)` coefficient reduces." "Commute `r²` and `g r` pointwise, then close the remaining coefficient identity with ring normalization."], :boundary "The theorem retains the downstream integrability hypothesis even though the underlying Bochner-integral identity is unconditional.", :capture-kind :runner-narrated-and-commit-witnessed, :witness {:declaration "ConstructionTargets.RadialIntegrationR3.radial_integral_R3", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false}, :target "∫ x : E, g ‖x‖ ∂volume = 4 * π * ∫ r in Ioi (0 : ℝ), g r * r ^ 2 ∂volume"}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdi