{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-package-closed-ball-holomorphicity-as-DiffContOnCl-for-Cauchy-estimates", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "When a complex-analysis theorem expects `DiffContOnCl`, adapt a closed-ball differentiability hypothesis by separating its three interfaces: differentiability on the open ball, continuity on the closed closure, and a sphere-local bound.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "package-closed-ball-holomorphicity-as-DiffContOnCl-for-Cauchy-estimates", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "When a complex-analysis theorem expects `DiffContOnCl`, adapt a closed-ball differentiability hypothesis by separating its three interfaces: differentiability on the open ball, continuity on the closed closure, and a sphere-local bound.", :body {:adapter ["Build the `DiffContOnCl` argument required by the Cauchy estimate." "For its differentiability field, restrict the closed-ball hypothesis to the open ball with `hg.mono ball_subset_closedBall`." "For continuity on the closure, use `hg.continuousOn` and normalize the closure with `closure_ball _ hρ.ne'`." "For the sphere norm bound, inherit the closed-ball bound through `sphere_subset_closedBall`." "Apply `norm_deriv_le_of_forall_mem_sphere_norm_le hρ` to obtain the estimate directly."], :capture-kind :runner-api-packaging-and-ground-control-verification, :key-api "Complex.norm_deriv_le_of_forall_mem_sphere_norm_le", :witness {:declaration "deriv_norm_le_sup_div_radius", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :statement-integrity :intact}, :rule "When a complex-analysis theorem expects `DiffContOnCl`, adapt a closed-ball differentiability hypothesis by separating its three interfaces: differentiability on the open ball, continuity on the closed closure, and a sphere-local bound.", :scope {:language :lean4, :problem "Apply Cauchy's derivative estimate when the available hypothesis is `DifferentiableOn ℂ g (closedBall z₀ ρ)` and the norm bound is stated on that closed ball."}, :boundary "This closes the derivative estimate only. The row's remaining disk-area mean-value inequality still needs radial integration, polar coordinates, and Fubini.", :lean-shape "apply norm_deriv_le_of_forall_mem_sphere_norm_le hρ\n    · constructor\n      · exact hg.mono ball_subset_closedBall\n      · simpa [closure_ball _ hρ.ne'] using hg.continuousOn\n    · exact fun w hw ↦ hM w (sphere_subset_closedBall hw)", :target "`‖deriv g z₀‖ ≤ M / ρ` for `0 < ρ` and `‖g w‖ ≤ M` on `closedBall z₀ ρ`."}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :arc-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T14:26:52.966457801Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-package-closed-ball-holomorphicity-as-DiffContOnCl-for-Cauchy-estimates"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-package-every-rouche-homotopy-slice-for-the-argument-principle", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "When a construction is blocked on a deep invariance theorem, first package all elementary hypotheses in the theorem's intended quantifier shape; this prevents the frontier from remaining entangled with routine analytic closure and boundary estimates.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Expose the exact analytic/topological input for Rouché's straight-line homotopy before attacking the argument-principle theorem.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "package-every-rouche-homotopy-slice-for-the-argument-principle", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "When a construction is blocked on a deep invariance theorem, first package all elementary hypotheses in the theorem's intended quantifier shape; this prevents the frontier from remaining entangled with routine analytic closure and boundary estimates.", :body {:hook "Before invoking zero-count invariance for `f + t·g`, package two facts for every `t ∈ [0,1]`: analyticity on the same closed-disk neighbourhood and nonvanishing on the boundary sphere.", :capture-kind :runner-axiom-clean-interface-package-and-ground-control-verification, :problem-class "Expose the exact analytic/topological input for Rouché's straight-line homotopy before attacking the argument-principle theorem.", :key-api ["AnalyticOnNhd.add" "AnalyticOnNhd.mul" "analyticOnNhd_const" "ConstructionTargets.Rouche.rouche_homotopy_ne_zero_on_sphere"], :relation-to-existing {:memory-id "e-codexpilot-straight-line-rouche-homotopy-stays-nonzero-on-boundary", :relation "That memory proves the pointwise boundary half. This record adds the common-neighbourhood analyticity of every slice and packages both hypotheses at the interface required by the remaining argument-principle bridge."}, :rule "When a construction is blocked on a deep invariance theorem, first package all elementary hypotheses in the theorem's intended quantifier shape; this prevents the frontier from remaining entangled with routine analytic closure and boundary estimates.", :boundary "The package does not prove zero-count invariance or Rouché's theorem. `zeroCountInClosedBall_add_eq` remains sorried.", :lean-detail "`AnalyticOnNhd.const_mul` was unavailable at this Mathlib revision. The compiling construction is `hf.add (analyticOnNhd_const.mul hg)`.", :how-to-apply ["Start from `hf : AnalyticOnNhd ℂ f s` and `hg : AnalyticOnNhd ℂ g s`." "For a real parameter `t`, prove analyticity of `z ↦ f z + (t : ℂ) * g z` with closure of `AnalyticOnNhd` under addition and multiplication by an analytic constant." "Use the strict boundary estimate `‖g z‖ < ‖f z‖` and `t ∈ [0,1]` to invoke the existing straight-line boundary-nonvanishing lemma." "Return the analytic and boundary facts as one conjunction indexed by `t : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1`." "Pass this packaged family directly to an argument-principle or zero-count homotopy-invariance theorem, keeping routine closure facts out of the missing bridge."], :declarations [{:name "ConstructionTargets.Rouche.rouche_homotopy_analyticOnNhd", :statement-shape "AnalyticOnNhd ℂ f s → AnalyticOnNhd ℂ g s → AnalyticOnNhd ℂ (fun z ↦ f z + (t : ℂ) * g z) s"} {:name "ConstructionTargets.Rouche.rouche_homotopy_analyticOnNhd_and_ne_zero", :statement-shape "For every `t ∈ [0,1]`, the slice is analytic near `closedBall c R` and nonzero on `sphere c R`."}], :axiom-audit {:declarations ["rouche_homotopy_analyticOnNhd" "rouche_homotopy_analyticOnNhd_and_ne_zero"], :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false}}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T2