{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-pair-a-machine-checked-refutation-with-a-machine-checked-statement-repair", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "For a false formal statement, the cheapest owner-review artifact is a checked counterexample plus a checked repaired sibling, with the original target preserved as an explicit unresolved defect.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "pair-a-machine-checked-refutation-with-a-machine-checked-statement-repair", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "For a false formal statement, the cheapest owner-review artifact is a checked counterexample plus a checked repaired sibling, with the original target preserved as an explicit unresolved defect.", :body {:boundary "A proved repair establishes internal consistency and sufficiency of the added hypothesis; adopting it may still require checking fidelity to the originating mathematical problem.", :capture-kind :runner-machine-checked-refutation-and-repair-demonstration, :rule "For a false formal statement, the cheapest owner-review artifact is a checked counterexample plus a checked repaired sibling, with the original target preserved as an explicit unresolved defect.", :observed-case {:problem "a94J02", :false-statement "`interior C = ∅` alone implies `constructedH C` is strictly monotone.", :counterexample "Take `C=[0,1]\\ℚ`; its complement inside the interval is countable, so the defining integral vanishes rather than becoming strictly monotone.", :refutation-declaration "constructedH_strictMonoOn_counterexample", :repair "Add `IsClosed C`; openness of the complement then supplies a positive-length subinterval between distinct points.", :repair-declaration "constructedH_strictMonoOn_of_isClosed", :status :both-axiom-clean}, :hook "When a target is false, leave it visibly unresolved while proving both an existential counterexample to the original quantification and the minimally repaired theorem.", :how-to-apply ["Negate the original universal statement at its real quantifier boundary rather than merely documenting an informal counterexample." "Construct a witness satisfying every stated hypothesis and prove the target conclusion fails." "Identify the missing hypothesis from the failure mechanism." "State and prove a repaired sibling theorem with that hypothesis added." "Leave the original false declaration unchanged and sorried, with a docstring pointing to the machine-checked refutation." "Report refutation and repair separately so the owner decides whether to adopt the new statement rather than whether the diagnosis is credible."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :trajectory-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-31T03:16:21.732744086Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-pair-a-machine-checked-refutation-with-a-machine-checked-statement-repair"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-place-section-include-after-a-definition-to-repair-theorems-without-changing-the-definition", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "Treat section context as syntactic until declaration signatures are inspected. Position `include` at the narrowest declaration boundary so a repair strengthens the intended theorems without contaminating an independent definition.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "place-section-include-after-a-definition-to-repair-theorems-without-changing-the-definition", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "Treat section context as syntactic until declaration signatures are inspected. Position `include` at the narrowest declaration boundary so a repair strengthens the intended theorems without contaminating an independent definition.", :body {:capture-kind :confirmed-falsehood-repair-and-load-bearing-proof-use, :rule "Treat section context as syntactic until declaration signatures are inspected. Position `include` at the narrowest declaration boundary so a repair strengthens the intended theorems without contaminating an independent definition.", :failure {:shape "Theorems were quantified over arbitrary `K`; `K = ∅` refuted the intended non-extension conclusion.", :cause "Lean does not automatically include unused section variables in a declaration."}, :headline-observation "Section variables `hK_compact` and `hK_measure` were declared but omitted from later theorem signatures because they were not referenced; adding `include` after `cauchyTransform` repaired those theorems while preserving the definition's signature.", :repair ["Keep `def cauchyTransform` before the `include` directive, preserving its signature." "Place `include hK_compact hK_measure` before the theorem declarations that semantically require them." "Verify the repaired hypotheses are load-bearing in the proof; `hK_compact` was used six times in the committed partial."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-9 2026-07-29/30; Joe's standing direction)", :review-note "Owner review: verified in the field, not merely proposed. a00J05's repair placed `include` AFTER `def cauchyTransform` precisely so the definition kept its `Set R -> C -> C` signature, and the subsequent run used hK_compact SIX times. The placement detail is the load-bearing part of this memory: including before the def would have changed the definition's arity and broken every use."}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :trajectory-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T10:08:58.865659679Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-9", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-place-section-include-after-a-definition-to-repair-theorems-without-changing-the-definition"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-poisson-ae-convergence-bridge", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:kind :reference, :name "poisson-ae-convergence-bridge", :hook "Tendsto (fun r ↦ ⨍ t in closedBall x r, ‖f t - f x‖ ∂volume)\n    (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 0) →\n  MemLp f 2 volume →\n  Tendsto\n    (fun y ↦ ∫ t, poissonKernel y (x - t) * (f t - f x) ∂volume)\n    (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 0)", :body {:statement "Tendsto (fun r ↦ ⨍ t in closedBall x r, ‖f t - f x‖ ∂volume)\n    (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 0) →\n  MemLp f 2 volume →\n  Tendsto\n    (fun y ↦ ∫ t, poissonKernel y (x - t) * (f t - f x) ∂volume)\n    (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 0)", :capture-kind :runner-verbatim-statement-and-literature-report, :demand-note "Ground control assigns demand 2 because the bridge gates the a.e. target and the campaign's preceding sorried `L²` convergence result.", :interpretation "At a Lebesgue point of an `L²` function, the Poisson convolution error tends to zero as the height approaches zero from above.", :route "Formalize the dyadic-annulus estimate for the near region, sum the annular bounds using the Lebesgue-point hypothesis, and control the far tail using `MemLp f 2 volume`; alternatively, provide suitable Poisson maximal-function control.", :boundary "Core Mathlib's compact-support approximate-identity theorem cannot establish this full-support Poisson statement, and the archived project does not supply a directly importable theorem at this interface.", :literature {:source "leanprover-community Zulip archive / Carleson project", :archive-path "442935-Carleson/Hardy-Littlewood.20maximal.20principle.20for.20countable.20many.20balls.json", :use-status :found-and-used, :contribution "The thread locates countable-family and weak/strong-type maximal-function infrastructure in the Carleson project rather than core Mathlib.", :thread "442935-Carleson/Hardy-Littlewood maximal principle for countable many balls"}, :frontier/kind :missing-proof, :unblocks [{:ref/type :lean-theorem, :ref/id "poissonConv_tendsto_ae"} {:ref/type :lean-theorem, :ref/id "poissonConv_tendsto_L2"}]}, :runner-model :codex, :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/cron-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :frontier-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-29T09:41:48.735988708Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-poisson-ae-convergence-bridge"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-prefer-installed-source-search-when-the-library-namespace-is-guessable", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:kind :feedback, :name "prefer-installed-source-search-when-the-library-namespace-is-guessable", :hook "prefer-installed-source-search-when-the-library-namespace-is-guessable", :body {:boundary "Three consecutive rows establish a useful lane-local trigger, not a global accuracy ranking of search tools. The observation concerns exact installed-revision APIs and guessable namespaces.", :capture-kind :three-row-search-surface-comparison-explicitly-inferred, :inference {:classification :three-instance-operational-inference, :trigger "The target can be translated into a plausible installed Mathlib namespace, structure name, or distinctive declaration fragment.", :policy ["Search the installed Mathlib source first with those exact tokens and nearby operation words." "Inspect neighbouring declarations and imports because the needed API often appears as a family rather than one semantic match." "Use Loogle or LeanSearch when the namespace or declaration vocabulary is not yet guessable, or to widen the search after local component search stalls."]}, :observed-sequence [{:problem "a03J08", :local-search-targets ["removable singularity" "punctured neighbourhood" "cocompact constancy"], :outcome "Local installed-source search found the finite-puncture and Liouville components; external declaration search did not carry the proof."} {:problem "a92J03", :local-search-targets ["Real.tendsto_integral_exp_smul_cocompact" "Filter.tendsto_cocompact_mul_left₀" "Real.fourierChar_apply"], :outcome "Local installed-source search found the complete Riemann--Lebesgue adapter API; external results were irrelevant."} {:problem "a92J04", :local-search-targets ["FormalMultilinearSeries" "HasFPowerSeriesAt" "ofScalars" "radius"], :outcome "Local installed-source search found every power-series component; external results were again irrelevant.