{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-preflight-file-elaboration-before-sorry-accounting-or-runner-dispatch", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "Treat successful elaboration of the exact target under its real project build as a precondition for proof-hole measurement and runner dispatch, and separate dependency-build failures from source-statement failures by rerunning after the dependency is built.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "preflight-file-elaboration-before-sorry-accounting-or-runner-dispatch", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "Treat successful elaboration of the exact target under its real project build as a precondition for proof-hole measurement and runner dispatch, and separate dependency-build failures from source-statement failures by rerunning after the dependency is built.", :body {:boundary "This preflight detects whether a row is formally runnable. It does not decide which semantic repair is faithful when an ill-typed statement admits several interpretations.", :capture-kind :runner-elaboration-diagnosis-and-owner-verified-repair-fork, :rule "Treat successful elaboration of the exact target under its real project build as a precondition for proof-hole measurement and runner dispatch, and separate dependency-build failures from source-statement failures by rerunning after the dependency is built.", :observed-case {:problem "a01J02", :failures ["`B ∈ borel ℝ` applies set-membership notation to a measurable-space value." "A subtype-domain function is paired with a measure on `ℝ`." "The symmetric-difference statement uses stale scope/API assumptions."], :semantic-risk "The literal repair makes the conclusions reflexive, while the intended completion theorem needs `NullMeasurableSet` and `AEMeasurable`; compilation repair therefore requires a mathematical choice."}, :hook "A sorry queue is not actionable until the exact target file elaborates: otherwise the runner is 