{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-refute-essential-boundedness-at-a-singularity-on-a-positive-measure-ball", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "To disprove an essential bound near a point singularity, thicken the violation to a positive-measure punctured neighbourhood; the exceptional point alone is invisible to `L∞`.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Show that a function singular at the origin does not belong to `L∞`, even though changing the value at the singleton origin cannot witness failure of an a.e. bound.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "refute-essential-boundedness-at-a-singularity-on-a-positive-measure-ball", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "To disprove an essential bound near a point singularity, thicken the violation to a positive-measure punctured neighbourhood; the exceptional point alone is invisible to `L∞`.", :body {:problem-class "Show that a function singular at the origin does not belong to `L∞`, even though changing the value at the singleton origin cannot witness failure of an a.e. bound.", :capture-kind :runner-proof-and-commit-witnessed, :rule "To disprove an essential bound near a point singularity, thicken the violation to a positive-measure punctured neighbourhood; the exceptional point alone is invisible to `L∞`.", :witness {:declaration "f_radial_not_memLp_top", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false}, :route ["Assume `MemLp f ⊤` and extract an a.e. finite norm bound." "Choose a sufficiently small radius from that bound." "On the punctured ball around zero, prove the singular profile exceeds the alleged bound." "Use positivity of the ball's volume and nullity of the singleton to obtain a positive-measure set on which the a.e. bound fails."], :lean-arcs ["Use `measure_singleton` rather than treating the singular point itself as positive-measure evidence." "Normalize distance with `dist_zero_right`." "Normalize reciprocal expressions through `one