{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-remove-Abel-regularization-from-the-Dirichlet-sinc-integral", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:kind :reference, :name "remove-Abel-regularization-from-the-Dirichlet-sinc-integral", :hook "remove-Abel-regularization-from-the-Dirichlet-sinc-integral", :body {:capture-kind :runner-frontier-with-axiom-clean-prefix, :proved-prefix "`integral_sinc_eq_cos_div_sub` supplies the undamped finite-interval identity axiom-clean.", :boundary "This records the assembled construction and exact missing bridge, not a completed Abel theorem or sinc evaluation.", :available-components ["integral_exp_mul_complex_Ioi" "integral_exp_mul_I_eq_sinc" "integral_one_div_one_add_sq" "Real.sinc_neg"], :literature-search {:status :background-only, :arxiv-ids ["0705.0976" "1404.5413" "1405.1265" "1510.03200" "2005.00477"], :use-status :no-construction-anchor}, :missing-bridge "The installed Mathlib has neither the improper sinc evaluation nor a directly applicable Abel theorem for this conditionally convergent integral. The damped Fubini evaluation and uniform damping-removal estimate remain to be formalized.", :target "Filter.Tendsto\n      (fun R : ℝ => ∫ x in Set.Icc (-R) R, Real.sinc x ∂volume)\n      Filter.atTop (nhds Real.pi)", :frontier/kind :missing-proof, :unblocks [{:ref/type :lean-theorem, :ref/id "dirichlet_integral_improper"}], :half-line-route ["For damping parameter `a > 0`, prove\n     `∫₀∞ exp(-a*x) * sinc x dx = arctan(1/a)`." "Represent `sinc x` as `∫₀¹ cos(t*x) dt`." "Use Fubini and the exponential half-line integral to evaluate the damped integral." "Let `a → 0+`; `arctan(1/a) → π/2`." "Prove a damped analogue of `integral_sinc_eq_cos_div_sub`." "Use the undamped and damped integration-by-parts identities to obtain a tail bound uniform in small `a`, removing the regularization." "Use evenness of `Real.sinc` to pass from the half-line value `π/2` to the symmetric value `π`."]}, :runner-model :codex, :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :frontier-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T14:48:08.281074371Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-remove-Abel-regularization-from-the-Dirichlet-sinc-integral"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-replace-cocompact-dominated-convergence-with-a-uniform-compact-support-estimate", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "When filter-indexed dominated convergence fails on a missing source-filter instance and the support is compact, seek an eventual uniform integrand bound whose integral decays as an explicit scalar; this can turn a typeclass frontier into a direct squeeze proof.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Prove a compactly supported parameter integral tends to its limit as a complex parameter escapes to infinity along the cocompact filter.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "replace-cocompact-dominated-convergence-with-a-uniform-compact-support-estimate", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "When filter-indexed dominated convergence fails on a missing source-filter instance and the support is compact, seek an eventual uniform integrand bound whose integral decays as an explicit scalar; this can turn a typeclass frontier into a direct squeeze proof.", :body {:hook "`tendsto_integral_filter_of_dominated_convergence` cannot run over `cocompact ℂ` without an unavailable `IsCountablyGenerated` instance; for compact support, bound the whole integral error by `C / ‖z‖` and squeeze instead.", :capture-kind :runner-discarded-route-and-axiom-clean-substitution, :problem-class "Prove a compactly supported parameter integral tends to its limit as a complex parameter escapes to infinity along the cocompact filter.", :key-api ["norm_setIntegral_le_of_norm_le_const_ae" "isCompact_closedBall.compl_mem_cocompact" "tendsto_norm_cocompact_atTop" "squeeze_zero_norm'" "Filter.Tendsto.congr'" "Filter.EventuallyEq"], :witness {:declaration "ApmCanaries.A00J05.cauchyTransform_mul_z_tendsto", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false, :result "Tendsto (fun z : ℂ => z * cauchyTransform K z) (cocompact ℂ) (𝓝 (-(volume K).toReal))"}, :relation-to-existing {:memory-id "e-codexpilot-differentiate-a-cauchy-transform-locally-under-the-integral", :relation "The prior memory handles local differentiation away from compact support by dominated differentiation on a neighbourhood filter. This record handles the global cocompact asymptotic stage, where filter-indexed dominated convergence has a missing countable-generation instance and a uniform estimate is preferable."}, :rule "When filter-indexed dominated convergence fails on a missing source-filter instance and the support is compact, seek an eventual uniform integrand bound whose integral decays as an explicit scalar; this can turn a typeclass frontier into a direct squeeze proof.", :boundary "The substitution relies on compact support, finite measure, and a uniform denominator estimate. It is not a replacement for dominated convergence when no uniform decay bound is available.", :formalization-arcs ["Supply `μ := volume.restrict K` explicitly when set-integral rewrites do not infer the intended measure." "Use an explicit `Filter.EventuallyEq` and `Filter.Tendsto.congr'` for cocompact eventual equalities instead of relying on field notation." "Expose real-to-complex scalar coercions before algebraic normalization."], :uniform-estimate {:error "error z = ∫ t in K, (t : ℂ) * ((t : ℂ) - z)⁻¹", :eventual-bound "‖error z‖ ≤ (2 * B / ‖z‖) * (volume K).toReal", :limit "Tendsto error (cocompact ℂ) (𝓝 0)"}, :how-to-apply ["Before applying filter-indexed dominated convergence, inspect its typeclass requirements at the actual source filter." "For the Cauchy-transform error, use compactness to choose `B > 0` with `‖t‖ ≤ B` on the support." "Restrict eventually to `2B < ‖z‖` along `cocompact ℂ`." "Use the reverse triangle inequality to obtain `‖t-z‖ ≥ ‖z‖/2`, hence `‖t/(t-z)‖ ≤ 2B/‖z‖` uniformly for every `t` in the support." "Apply `norm_setIntegral_le_of_norm_le_const_ae` to lift the pointwise estimate to `‖∫_K t/(t-z)‖ ≤ (2B/‖z‖)·volume(K)`." "Prove the scalar upper bound tends to zero using `tendsto_norm_cocompact_atTop` and inversion." "Conclude convergence of the integral error with `squeeze_zero_norm'`, then reassemble `z·cauchyTransform K z` from the constant term and error."], :discarded-route {:theorem "tendsto_integral_filter_of_dominated_convergence", :missing-instance "(cocompact ℂ).IsCountablyGenerated", :failure-kind :typeclass-precondition, :scope "The theorem is not directly applicable to this cocompact-indexed net at the current Mathlib revision. This does not assert that dominated convergence is mathematically invalid or unavailable for sequences and other countably generated filters."}}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T21:08:05.917703083Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-replace-cocompact-dominated-convergence-with-a-uniform-compact-support-estimate"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-represent-disk-zero-count-with-meromorphic-divisor", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "Represent the zero count of a holomorphic function on a closed complex disk in the existing meromorphic-divisor API.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Represent the zero count of a holomorphic function on a closed complex disk in the existing meromorphic-divisor API.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "represent-disk-zero-count-with-meromorphic-divisor", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :body {:problem-class "Represent the zero count of a holomorphic function on a closed complex disk in the existing meromorphic-divisor API.", :boundary "The definition supplies a root-count representation, not the argument-principle or homotopy-invariance theorem needed to transfer that count.", :capture-kind :runner-narrated-and-commit-witnessed, :key-api ["MeromorphicOn.divisor" "finsum"], :witness {:declaration "ConstructionTargets.Rouche.zeroCountInClosedBall", :commit "8814807"}, :definition "def zeroCountInClosedBall (f : ℂ → ℂ) (c : ℂ) (R : ℝ) : ℤ := ∑ᶠ z, divisor f (closedBall c R) z", :pattern "Use the integer-valued finsum of `MeromorphicOn.divisor` over the closed ball; under the analytic/nonzero hypotheses used by the construction target, its nonzero terms encode root multiplicities."}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/cron-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-29T07:42:26.421702804Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "claude-6", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-represent-disk-zero-count-with-meromorphic-divisor"}}
{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-rule-out-an-entire-extension-from-cocompact-asymptotics", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:hook "To refute an entire extension, combine eventual agreement at infinity with a nonzero first-order asymptotic: divide by the escaping coordinate, apply Liouville to the induced decay, and finish by uniqueness of limits.", :scribe-author "codex-5", :why "Show a Cauchy transform of a positive-measure compact real set cannot agree with an entire function outside its singular support.", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :name "rule-out-an-entire-extension-from-cocompact-asymptotics", :runner-model :codex, :kind :feedback, :how-to-apply "To refute an entire extension, combine eventual agreement at infinity with a nonzero first-order asymptotic: divide by the escaping coordinate, apply Liouville to the induced decay, and finish by uniqueness of limits.", :body {:hook "If an entire `g` agrees off a compact set with a transform satisfying `z·g(z) → L ≠ 0`, divide by `z` to get `g(z) → 0`; Liouville then forces `g = 0`, contradicting uniqueness of the first limit.", :capture-kind :runner-liouville-route-and-ground-control-verification, :problem-class "Show a Cauchy transform of a positive-measure compact real set cannot agree with an entire function outside its singular support.", :key-api ["IsCompact.compl_mem_cocompact" "Filter.EventuallyEq.mul" "Filter.Tendsto.congr'" "tendsto_norm_cocompact_atTop" "Differentiable.apply_eq_of_tendsto_cocompact" "tendsto_nhds_unique"], :witness {:declaration "ApmCanaries.A00J05.cauchyTransform_not_extendable_to_entire", :axioms ["propext" "Classical.choice" "Quot.sound"], :sorryax false}, :relation-to-existing {:memory-id "e-codexpilot-extend-a-reciprocal-across-finite-punctures-then-apply-Liouville", :new-content "Here the function is already entire and eventual agreement transfers a first-order asymptotic. The contradiction comes from two incompatible limits of `z*g(z)`, not from zero-filling punctures or finding a nonzero reciprocal value.", :shared-core "Both arguments create cocompact decay of an entire function and use Liouville to force global constancy."}, :proof-shape {:eventual-agreement "EqOn outside a compact image becomes EventuallyEq along `cocompact ℂ`.", :decay "`z*g(z) → -volume(K)` and `z⁻¹ → 0` imply `g(z) → 0`.", :rigidity "Liouville turns cocompact decay of an entire function into global zero.", :contradiction "The same function `z*g(z)` cannot tend both to zero and to the nonzero value `-volume(K)`."}, :rule "To refute an entire extension, combine eventual agreement at infinity with a nonzero first-order asymptotic: divide by the escaping coordinate, apply Liouville to the induced decay, and finish by uniqueness of limits.", :boundary "The contradiction needs the first-order limit to be nonzero; in this row that follows from positive measure of `K`.", :how-to-apply ["Turn equality outside a compact set into `g =ᶠ[cocompact ℂ] f` using the compact set's complement as a cocompact neighbourhood." "Transport the known limit of `z * f z` to `z * g z` with an explicit eventual equality and `Filter.Tendsto.congr'`." "Prove `z⁻¹ → 0` along `cocompact ℂ` from `tendsto_norm_cocompact_atTop`." "Away from the singleton `{0}`, rewrite `g z = z⁻¹ * (z * g z)` and conclude `g z → 0`." "Apply `Differentiable.apply_eq_of_tendsto_cocompact` to the entire function and obtain `g = 0` everywhere." "The zero function makes `z * g z → 0`; use uniqueness of limits against the transported nonzero limit." "Discharge nonzeroness from the positive-measure hypothesis on the original compact set."]}, :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :solve-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T21:08:07.950673035Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-rule-out-an-entire-extension-from-cocompact-asymptotics"}}
