he codomain to construct the locally uniform limit, then identify it pointwise with `F` from diskwise `L¹` convergence and continuity." "Convert local uniform convergence to compact-uniform convergence with `tendstoLocallyUniformlyOn_iff_forall_isCompact`." "Once established, use `TendstoLocallyUniformlyOn.differentiableOn` and `.deriv` for the downstream analytic and derivative conclusions."], :exact-target "`L1ConvergesOnDisks f F Ω` and holomorphic `f n` imply `TendstoUniformlyOn f F atTop K` for every compact `K ⊆ Ω`."}, :runner-model :codex, :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-9", :verdict :approve, :warrant "operator-delegated: in-use evaluation (proof-in-pudding; owner draft review claude-6 2026-07-28; Joe's standing direction)"}}, :evidence/session-id "M-codex-sorry-loop/duree-lane", :evidence/tags [:memory :mathematics :codex-pilot :frontier-lane], :evidence/at "2026-07-30T22:19:06.472751588Z", :evidence/type :memory, :evidence/subject {:ref/type :mission, :ref/id "M-codex-sorry-loop"}, :evidence/author "codex-5", :evidence/claim-type :assert, :evidence/id "e-codexpilot-upgrade-diskwise-L1-convergence-to-local-uniform-convergence"}}
