{:record/kind :evidence, :record/id "e-codexpilot-zeroCountInClosedBall-homotopy-invariant", :record/payload {:evidence/body {:kind :reference, :name "zeroCountInClosedBall-homotopy-invariant", :hook "zeroCountInClosedBall_homotopy_invariant\n  (F : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1 → ℂ → ℂ)\n  (hF : ∀ t, AnalyticOnNhd ℂ (F t) (closedBall c R))\n  (hboundary : ∀ t z, z ∈ sphere c R → F t z ≠ 0) :\n  zeroCountInClosedBall (F 1) c R =\n    zeroCountInClosedBall (F 0) c R", :body {:boundary "The committed file proves the straight-line boundary nonvanishing lemmas but leaves this bridge as the sole `sorry`; the archive anchor does not itself provide the missing Lean theorem.", :capture-kind :runner-narrated, :statement "zeroCountInClosedBall_homotopy_invariant\n  (F : Set.Icc (0 : ℝ) 1 → ℂ → ℂ)\n  (hF : ∀ t, AnalyticOnNhd ℂ (F t) (closedBall c R))\n  (hboundary : ∀ t z, z ∈ sphere c R → F t z ≠ 0) :\n  zeroCountInClosedBall (F 1) c R =\n    zeroCountInClosedBall (F 0) c R", :frontier/kind :missing-proof, :literature {:source "leanprover-community Zulip archive", :runner-locator "116395-maths/Argument principle.json", :archive-path "116395-maths/Argument.20principle.json", :use-status :found-and-used, :contribution "The thread identified the argument-principle/residue/winding-number infrastructure as the relevant bridge and warned that older Mathlib lacked a ready theorem."}, :unblocks [{:ref/type :lean-theorem, :ref/id "zeroCountInClosedBall_add_eq"} {:ref/type :apm-problem, :ref/id "a92J05"}], :route "Supply the argument-principle bridge showing that the total divisor inside the disk is invariant under an analytic homotopy that remains nonzero on the boundary.", :near-miss "`Complex.JensenFormula` is available, but its identity weights the divisor by radius/distance and does not state invariance of the unweighted total zero multiplicity."}, :runner-model :codex, :scribe-author "codex-5", :draft-source "holes/labs/M-codex-sorry-loop/", :promotion {:reviewed-by "claude-6", :verdict :app